      "name": "CopyDataWithLookup",
      "signature": "void CopyDataWithLookup(byte * pbSrcData, byte * pbDestData, dword nTableOffset, dword nCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Copies packed data items to destination buffer using lookup table for decompression.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each of nCount data items, read variable-length header (offset, length pair, 2 bytes)\n2. If both bytes are zero, skip item and advance to next position (stride g_dwStrideIncrement)\n3. Otherwise: compute destination write position = pbDestData + offset; copy length bytes from source using table lookup at base nTableOffset\n4. Lookup mechanism: for each source byte, read it as index into lookup table and write result to destination\n5. Repeat until all nCount items processed\n\nParameters:\n- pbSrcData (byte*): Packed source buffer containing offset/length pairs followed by indices\n- pbDestData (byte*): Output buffer where decompressed data is written\n- nTableOffset (int): Base address/offset into lookup table (added to each source byte as index)\n- nCount (int): Number of data items to process; inner loop decrements\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero offset and zero length: Skip item, use stride to find next item\n- Variable copy length: Handled by switch fallthrough (1-32 byte copy), uses __d2mixcall convention\n- Lookup table: Assumes table is readable via addition of source byte to nTableOffset base",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f728acdacf50da6a49c5bb46e9493516",
