      "name": "DrawRowPixelsWithPalette",
      "signature": "void DrawRowPixelsWithPalette(int nDelta, int nYPos, byte * pbSource, int nXPos, int nPalOffset, int nCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Renders a row of palette-indexed pixels with clipping and row-strided output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize destination X position and row counter\n2. For each input row, read 2-byte entry (flags and width)\n3. If both bytes are zero, increment row counter and stride X position\n4. Otherwise, calculate destination bounds with palette offset applied\n5. Clip bytes to valid window bounds, compute gap from clipping\n6. Copy clipped bytes with palette offset using fall-through switch (Duff's device)\n7. Continue until all rows processed\n\nParameters:\n- nDelta (ECX): X position delta for stride adjustment\n- nYPos (EDX): Current Y position in output surface\n- pbSource (Stack[0x4]): Input row data (2-byte entries)\n- nXPos (Stack[0x8]): Starting X position for output\n- nPalOffset (Stack[0xc]): Palette index offset for all pixels\n- nCount (Stack[0x10]): Number of rows to process\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20: Maximum single copy block size (Duff's device)\n- 0x1f-0x0: Fall-through switch cases for remaining bytes\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Called by DrawRowPixelsWithPalette callers (FUN_6faa2910, FUN_6faa3150)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:8e3d91d07f3c7e3fa90cbe327cafa4e7",
