      "name": "RenderTileLineWithBlend",
      "signature": "void RenderTileLineWithBlend(int nXOffset, int nYOffset, byte * pbSourceLine, int nXPos, int nYPos, int nXDelta, int nYDelta, int nXInc, int nYInc, byte byShift)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Renders a single line of tile data with color blending.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate initial blend lookup table pointer based on tile position\n2. Loop through source line pixels, processing two-byte pixel pairs\n3. For zero-valued pixels (0x0000), skip output and advance pointers\n4. For non-zero pixels, copy blended colors via lookup table to output buffer\n5. Use fall-through switch for variable-length pixel blitting (up to 32 bytes)\n6. Handle clipping at tile boundaries when Y position exceeds screen limit\n\nParameters:\n- nXOffset (ECX): Horizontal offset for pixel operations\n- nYOffset (EDX): Vertical offset for pixel operations\n- pbSourceLine: Pointer to source tile pixel data (two bytes per pixel)\n- nXPos: Current X position in destination surface\n- nYPos: Current Y position in destination surface\n- nXDelta: X movement delta per iteration\n- nYDelta: Y movement delta per iteration\n- nXInc: X increment value\n- nYInc: Y increment value\n- byShift: Bit shift amount for tile coordinate calculations\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Maximum pixel data copy length\n- 0x1f (31): Highest offset in pixel copy sequence\n- 0x100: Color palette lookup multiplier",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
