      "name": "InitializeTileBlendLookup",
      "signature": "void InitializeTileBlendLookup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the tile blend lookup table with Gouraud shading color interpolation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize lookup table starting at g_pbTileBlendLookup\n2. For each row (0x20 rows, 0x400 bytes each):\n   - For each column (0x20 columns, 0x1000000 intensity step):\n     - For each pixel in column (0x20 pixels):\n       - Clamp intensity value to valid range [0, 0x1f000000]\n       - Store high byte (color intensity) to lookup table\n       - Advance to next interpolation step\n3. Write configuration values to global render state globals\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: No parameters passed (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies globals: g_pbTileBlendLookup, DAT_6fab4658, DAT_6fabd200, etc.)",
