      "name": "InitializeScreenDimensions",
      "signature": "void InitializeScreenDimensions(int nWidth, int nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes screen rendering dimensions and clipping bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Conditionally adjust width based on rendering mode (DAT_6fabd218)\n2. Calculate and store max Y coordinate (height - 0x2f)\n3. Store width/height to multiple global dimension arrays\n4. Initialize screen bounds and rendering state variables\n\nParameters:\n- nWidth (ECX): Screen width in pixels\n- nHeight (EDX): Screen height in pixels\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2f (47): Y offset for max coordinate calculation\n- 0x3f (63): Secondary Y offset\n- 0x20 (32): Standard size decrement\n- 0xf, 0xffffe0, etc: Boundary masks for clipping regions",
