      "name": "RenderTileDispatcher",
      "signature": "void RenderTileDispatcher(byte * pbTileData, int nXOffset, int nYOffset, byte * pbParams)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Dispatches tile rendering to appropriate render function based on mode and tile complexity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwSimpleRenderMode (DAT_6fabd214) for simple render mode flag\n2. If simple mode enabled:\n   a. Read first byte of params as control byte (bVar1)\n   b. If (controlByte & 0xF8) == 0xF8, call DrawSpriteClipped\n   c. Otherwise call DrawPixelRow with palette index\n3. If normal mode:\n   a. Extract tile coordinates from params structure:\n      - iVar3 = params[0] (tile X1)\n      - iVar2 = params[4] (tile Y1)  \n      - nXDelta = params[12] - params[0] (X delta)\n      - nXInc = params[8] - params[4] (Y delta)\n   b. Calculate complexity (iVar4) as sum of absolute deltas\n   c. If g_dwFlagState set OR complexity < 10, use simple render path\n   d. Otherwise use full tile render with bounds checking\n4. For full render path:\n   a. Validate coordinates against clip bounds (BoundMask2, MaxY, ClipY, ScreenDim)\n   b. Assert g_dwInitializationCounter is non-zero\n   c. Calculate destination buffer (pbDestBuffer) from row offset table\n   d. If within inner clip bounds, call DecodeScanlineRLE (fast path)\n   e. Otherwise call RenderTileLineWithBlend (clipped path)\n5. For simple render path with nYPos check:\n   a. If (nYPos >> 8) == 0x1F, call DrawSpriteClipped\n   b. Otherwise call DrawPixelRow\n\nParameters:\n  pbTileData (byte*, ECX): Pointer to tile pixel/RLE data\n  nXOffset (int, EDX): X screen coordinate for tile placement\n  nYOffset (int, Stack+4): Y screen coordinate for tile placement\n  pbParams (byte*, Stack+8): Pointer to tile parameters structure (16 bytes):\n    +0x00: int tile X1 coordinate\n    +0x04: int tile Y1 coordinate\n    +0x08: int tile X2 coordinate\n    +0x0C: int tile Y2 coordinate\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nDecompiler Variables:\n  bVar1: Control byte read from pbParams[0] for sprite type detection\n  iVar2: Tile Y1 coordinate from params[4]\n  iVar3: Tile X1 coordinate from params[0], reused as abs(Y1-X1)\n  iVar4: abs(nXInc), then reused as total complexity sum\n  iVar5: abs(nXDelta) for complexity calculation\n  nYPos: X1 << 5 (scaled X coordinate)\n  nXDelta: params[12] - params[0] (X span)\n  nXInc: params[8] - params[4] (Y span)\n  pbDestBuffer: Calculated destination in screen buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if g_dwInitializationCounter is 0 (buffer not initialized)\n  - Early returns if coordinates outside clip bounds\n  - Complexity threshold of 10 determines simple vs full render\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 (32): Tile size in pixels, left shift for coordinate scaling\n  0x08: Bit shift for tile addressing in RLE functions\n  0xF8: Mask for sprite type detection (bits 7-3)\n  0x1F00: Comparison for sprite clipping mode (nYPos >> 8 == 0x1F)\n  0x0A (10): Complexity threshold for render path selection\n  0x3BE (958): Source line number for assertion\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_dwSimpleRenderMode (DAT_6fabd214): Simple render mode flag\n  g_dwFlagState: Additional render mode flag at 0x6faae198\n  g_dwBoundMask2: Minimum Y clip bound\n  g_dwMaxY: Maximum Y clip bound  \n  g_dwClipY: Minimum X clip bound\n  g_dwScreenDim: Maximum X clip bound\n  g_dwInitializationCounter: Buffer initialization flag/base\n  g_aRowOffsetTable: Row offset lookup table\n  g_dwOffset2, g_dwMaxYPos3: Inner Y clip bounds\n  g_dwClipWidth, g_dwClipMinX2: Inner X clip bounds",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:fe60260a72ed86592727de9bfd440045",
