      "name": "RenderBlendedTileWithClipping",
      "signature": "void RenderBlendedTileWithClipping(byte * pbRleData, int nScreenX, int nScreenY, int * pnTileCoords, byte byBlendMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Renders a blended tile to the screen buffer with clipping support.\n\nDecodes RLE-compressed tile data and blends each pixel using a lookup table\nbased on the blend mode. Supports two rendering paths: an optimized path\nwhen the tile is fully within screen bounds, and a clipped path with\nboundary checking for partially visible tiles.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Select blend table pointer based on byBlendMode threshold:\n   - byBlendMode >= 0xC0: Use g_pSourceData[0] (full blend)\n   - byBlendMode >= 0x80: Use g_pSourceData[1] (medium blend)\n   - byBlendMode >= 0x40: Use g_pSourceData[2] (light blend)\n   - byBlendMode < 0x40: Early return (no rendering)\n2. Calculate tile coordinate deltas from pnTileCoords array:\n   - nDeltaX = pnTileCoords[3] - pnTileCoords[0]\n   - nDeltaY = pnTileCoords[2] - pnTileCoords[1]\n   - Multiply base coords by 32 (<<5) for fixed-point math\n3. Validate screen position against clipping bounds:\n   - g_dwBoundMask2 <= nScreenY < g_dwMaxY\n   - g_dwClipY <= nScreenX < g_dwScreenDim\n4. Assert g_dwInitializationCounter is non-zero\n5. Calculate destination buffer pointer from row offset table\n6. Calculate initial blend lookup table offset from fixed-point coords\n7. Choose rendering path:\n   - Optimized: tile fully within inner clip bounds\n   - Clipped: tile intersects screen edges\n8. Process 32 rows (0x20) of RLE data:\n   - Read skip count and pixel count from RLE stream\n   - If both zero: advance to next row\n   - Otherwise: blend pixels using two-stage lookup:\n     a. First lookup: g_pOutputBuffer[srcPixel + blendIdx * 256]\n     b. Second lookup: blendTable[dstPixel + intermediate * 256]\n\nParameters:\npbRleData - Pointer to RLE-encoded tile pixel data\nnScreenX  - Screen X coordinate (column) for tile placement\nnScreenY  - Screen Y coordinate (row) for tile placement\npnTileCoords - Array of 4 ints [baseX, baseY, endY, endX] for texture coords\nbyBlendMode - Blend intensity selector (0x40-0xFF valid range)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- byBlendMode < 0x40: Function returns immediately without rendering\n- g_dwInitializationCounter == 0: Triggers assertion and Exit(-1)\n- Tile outside screen bounds: Returns without rendering\n- Row with skip=0, count=0: Advances to next row without pixel operations\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x20 - Number of rows in tile (32 pixels tall)\n0x40 - Minimum blend mode threshold for light blend\n0x80 - Blend mode threshold for medium blend\n0xC0 - Blend mode threshold for full blend\n0x100 - Color table stride (256 entries per intensity level)\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\ng_pSourceData - Array of 3 blend table base addresses\ng_dwInitializationCounter - Base address of destination buffer\ng_aRowOffsetTable - Row stride lookup table\ng_pbTileBlendLookup - Tile-to-screen blend mapping table\ng_pOutputBuffer - Source pixel color mapping table\ng_dwStrideIncrement - Bytes per row in destination buffer",
