      "name": "InitializeGraphicsSystem",
      "signature": "dword InitializeGraphicsSystem(dword hInstance, dword lpfnWndProc, int nVideoMode, dword dwVideoParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the Diablo II graphics system and registers the main window class.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Build WNDCLASSA structure with window style (CS_OWNDC if not mode 5)\n2. Store hInstance and lpfnWndProc in global variables\n3. Load application icon (IDI_APPLICATION 0x67), arrow cursor (IDC_ARROW 0x7F00), and hollow brush\n4. Register window class with class name \"Diablo II\"\n5. If RegisterClassA fails, call DisplayGfxError and return 0 (or trigger fatal error)\n6. Call InitializeGame() and InitializeVideoMode() for game setup\n7. Store video mode parameters in globals\n8. Validate video mode index against g_apszVideoModeDllNames array\n9. LoadLibraryA the appropriate graphics DLL (D2DDraw.dll, D2Direct3D.dll, etc.)\n10. GetProcAddress ordinal 0x2710 (10000) to get graphics interface factory\n11. Call factory to get graphics interface vtable pointer\n12. Call interface method at offset 0x30 (setup) then offset 0x00 (init)\n13. If init fails, report error via ReportExceptionContext\n14. Set color depth to 0 if video mode < 4\n15. Call interface method at offset 0x04 and return result\n\nParameters:\n- hInstance (HINSTANCE): Application instance handle for window registration\n- lpfnWndProc (WNDPROC): Window procedure callback for message handling\n- nVideoMode (int): Video mode selector (0-5 indexing DLL name array)\n- dwVideoParam (dword): Additional video parameter stored globally\n\nReturns:\n- Non-zero: Success (graphics interface initialized)\n- 0: Failure (registration failed, DLL not found, or init failed)\n\nVideo Mode DLLs (g_apszVideoModeDllNames):\n- Mode 0-3: Software renderers\n- Mode 4+: Hardware accelerated (enables color depth)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x67: IDI_APPLICATION icon resource ID\n- 0x7F00: IDC_ARROW cursor resource ID\n- 5: HOLLOW_BRUSH stock object\n- 0x20: CS_OWNDC window class style\n- 0x2710: Ordinal 10000 for graphics interface factory\n- 0x73 (115): Source file line for DLL not found error\n- 0x7B (123): Source file line for GetProcAddress error\n\nError Handling:\n- RegisterClassA failure: DisplayGfxError then return 0 or INT3 fatal\n- LoadLibraryA failure: FogFatalError with DLL name, then Exit(-1)\n- GetProcAddress failure: FogFatalError with error code, then Exit(-1)\n- Graphics init failure: ReportExceptionContext with code 9",
