      "name": "VIDEO_IsHighResolutionMode",
      "signature": "bool VIDEO_IsHighResolutionMode(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Checks if the video mode is greater than 3 (higher resolution mode).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve the global video mode value\n2. Compare against threshold of 3\n3. Return true if mode > 3, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: None (no parameters)\n\nReturns:\n- true (1) if video mode is 4 or higher\n- false (0) if video mode is 3 or lower\n\nRelated:\n- Used to determine graphics capability level\n- Video mode >= 4 indicates high-resolution support",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
