      "name": "ToggleExpansionMode",
      "signature": "void ToggleExpansionMode(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Inverts the expansion mode toggle flag (800x600 vs 640x480 resolution mode).\n\nClassification: Leaf function - simple state toggle with no calls\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current expansion mode flag from g_fExpansionMode\n2. Test if flag is non-zero\n3. Set result to 1 if zero, 0 if non-zero (logical NOT via SETZ)\n4. Store inverted value back to g_fExpansionMode\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies global state only)\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_fExpansionMode (0x6faae190): Expansion mode flag (0=classic 640x480, 1=expansion 800x600)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10010: Returns expansion flag if color depth initialized\n- SetToggleState (Ordinal_10011): Sets the toggle value directly\n- SetScreenSize: Reads flag to determine screen dimensions\n- ValidateCoordinateRange: Uses flag for coordinate bounds\n- InitializeGraphicsSystem: Initializes the flag during startup\n\nMemory Model:\n- No allocations, reads/writes single global DWORD\n- Thread-safe only if called from single thread",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:0246ba23d2e2a9bb9388cd8cc7c4cceb",
