      "name": "GetExpansionModeIfInitialized",
      "signature": "uint GetExpansionModeIfInitialized(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Returns the expansion mode toggle value if graphics system is initialized.\n\nClassification: Leaf function, Public API (exported as D2GFX.Ordinal_10010)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load color depth value from g_dwColorDepth\n2. Load expansion mode toggle from g_dwExpansionModeToggle\n3. Check if color depth is non-zero (graphics initialized)\n4. If initialized, return toggle value; otherwise return 0\n\nThe NEG;SBB;AND pattern is a branchless optimization:\n- NEG sets CF if value was non-zero\n- SBB EAX,EAX produces -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) if CF set, 0 otherwise\n- AND masks the toggle value, returning it only if initialized\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- uint: g_dwExpansionModeToggle value if g_dwColorDepth != 0\n- uint: 0 if graphics not initialized (g_dwColorDepth == 0)\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n- g_dwColorDepth (0x6faae194): Graphics color depth, non-zero when initialized\n- g_dwExpansionModeToggle (0x6faae190): Expansion mode state flag\n\nExport: D2GFX.Ordinal_10010 - This function IS the ordinal export",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:af413c75688c051388954706b235eefd",
