      "name": "GFX_ToggleFlagState",
      "signature": "void GFX_ToggleFlagState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Toggles the global graphics flag state between 0 and 1.\n\nClassification: Public API (Ordinal 10015) - Graphics module state toggle\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current flag value from g_dwFlagState (0x6faae198)\n2. Test if current value is zero using TEST ECX,ECX\n3. Set AL to 1 if zero flag set (value was 0), else set AL to 0\n4. Store the inverted boolean result back to g_dwFlagState\n\nParameters:\n- None (operates on global state only)\n\nReturns:\n- void (result stored in global, no return value)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GFX_GetFlagState (Ordinal 10016): Returns current flag value\n- GFX_SetFlagState (Ordinal 10017): Sets flag to specified value\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- g_dwFlagState (0x6faae198): Graphics module state flag (0 or 1)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:0246ba23d2e2a9bb9388cd8cc7c4cceb",
