      "signature": "void GfxInterface_CallMethod0xA8(int nParam1, char cParam2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Invokes graphics interface method at vtable offset 0xA8.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - thin dispatch to graphics interface vtable.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global graphics interface pointer from g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c)\n2. Read function pointer at vtable offset 0xA8\n3. Call the method with two stack parameters\n4. Return (cleanup 8 bytes per __stdcall)\n\nParameters:\n- nParam1 (int): First parameter passed through to interface method\n- cParam2 (char): Second parameter passed through to interface method\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nCallers:\n- Referenced from 6faad164 and entry point (export table)\n\nRelated:\n- g_pGfxInterface @ 0x6fabd21c: Global graphics interface vtable pointer\n- Sibling functions: GfxInterface_CallMethod0x28, 0x4C, 0x5C dispatch to other vtable offsets\n\nNotes:\n- Exported as Ordinal 10051 from D2Gfx.dll\n- Part of graphics interface dispatch layer",
