      "name": "GfxInterface_CallMethod0xB0",
      "signature": "void GfxInterface_CallMethod0xB0(uint dwParam1, byte byParam2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Thunk wrapper that invokes GfxInterface vtable method at offset 0xB0.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - forwards call to graphics interface method\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pGfxInterface global pointer from 0x6fabd21c\n2. Load dwParam1 from stack offset +4 into ECX\n3. Load byParam2 from stack offset +8 into DL\n4. Call virtual method at vtable offset 0xB0 (176 bytes)\n5. Return with stack cleanup of 8 bytes (__stdcall)\n\nParameters:\n  dwParam1 (uint) - First parameter, passed in ECX to vtable method\n  byParam2 (byte) - Second parameter, passed in DL to vtable method\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value from this thunk\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Assumes g_pGfxInterface is valid and initialized by InitializeGraphicsSystem\n  No null check performed on g_pGfxInterface before dereference\n\nRelated Functions:\n  GfxInterface_CallMethod0xA8 - Similar thunk at vtable offset 0xA8\n  GfxInterface_CallMethod0xAC - Similar thunk at vtable offset 0xAC\n  InitializeGraphicsSystem - Initializes g_pGfxInterface global",
