      "name": "GfxSetClipRectangle",
      "signature": "void GfxSetClipRectangle(int nMinX, int nMinY, int nMaxX, int nMaxY, uint dwWidth, uint dwHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Sets the clipping rectangle for graphics rendering operations.\n\nExported as Ordinal 10056 in D2Gfx.dll.\n\nClassification: Worker function - validates coordinates and delegates to GFX interface\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load nMinX and nMaxX coordinates\n2. Validate nMaxX >= nMinX (exit if invalid rectangle width)\n3. Load nMinY and nMaxY coordinates  \n4. Validate nMaxY >= nMinY (exit if invalid rectangle height)\n5. Call GFX interface method 0xBC (SetClipRect) with validated coordinates\n\nParameters:\n  nMinX (int) - Left edge of clipping rectangle (X minimum)\n  nMinY (int) - Top edge of clipping rectangle (Y minimum)\n  nMaxX (int) - Right edge of clipping rectangle (X maximum)\n  nMaxY (int) - Bottom edge of clipping rectangle (Y maximum)\n  dwWidth (uint) - Width parameter for clip operation\n  dwHeight (uint) - Height parameter for clip operation\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if nMaxX < nMinX (invalid rectangle width)\n  - Early exit if nMaxY < nMinY (invalid rectangle height)\n  - No error code returned for invalid coordinates\n\nGFX Interface Method:\n  Offset 0xBC in g_pGfxInterface vtable - SetClipRect operation\n  Parameters passed: nMaxX, nMaxY, dwWidth, dwHeight",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
