      "name": "GfxInterface_CallMethod0x78",
      "signature": "void GfxInterface_CallMethod0x78(uint dwParam1, uint dwParam2, uint dwParam3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Graphics interface vtable method wrapper. Calls function at offset 0x78 (index 30) in g_pGfxInterface vtable with three parameters.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - passes parameters to vtable method\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load dwParam3 from stack into EAX\n2. Load dwParam2 from stack into EDX  \n3. Load dwParam1 from stack into ECX\n4. Push EAX (dwParam3) onto stack for callee\n5. Load g_pGfxInterface base pointer\n6. Call function pointer at [g_pGfxInterface + 0x78]\n7. Return with 12-byte stack cleanup (stdcall)\n\nParameters:\n- dwParam1 (uint): First graphics parameter, passed to callee in ECX\n- dwParam2 (uint): Second graphics parameter, passed to callee in EDX\n- dwParam3 (uint): Third graphics parameter, pushed on stack for callee\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nCalling Convention:\n- This function: __stdcall (cleans 12 bytes on RET)\n- Target method: Uses ECX, EDX registers plus stack param (custom/fastcall hybrid)\n\nVtable Reference:\n- g_pGfxInterface @ 0x6fabd21c\n- Method offset: 0x78 (vtable index 30, assuming 4-byte pointers)\n\nCross-References:\n- Called from export table (Ordinal 10050)\n- Referenced from data at 0x6faad160",
