      "name": "GfxCallInterfaceMethod",
      "signature": "void GfxCallInterfaceMethod(uint dwInterfaceId, uint dwParam2, uint dwParam3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Invokes a graphics interface method through function pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load method parameters from stack (dwInterfaceId, dwParam2, dwParam3)\n2. Calculate return address from ESP + 0x10\n3. Retrieve global graphics interface pointer (g_pGfxInterface)\n4. Call method at offset 0xc8 (200 bytes) with dwParam3 and return address\n\nParameters:\n- dwInterfaceId (uint): Interface or context identifier\n- dwParam2 (uint): Second parameter for the interface method\n- dwParam3 (uint): Third parameter, passed to called method\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Uses g_pGfxInterface global graphics interface pointer\n- Calls method at offset 0xc8 within the interface structure",
