      "name": "GfxDrawAndUpdateFrameIndex",
      "signature": "void GfxDrawAndUpdateFrameIndex(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Updates the frame index tracking and invokes the graphics interface draw handler.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - tail calls graphics draw routine\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current frame index from g_dwCurrentFrameIndex (0x6faae48c)\n2. Store current frame index into g_dwGameFlags (0x6faae490) as previous frame\n3. Load graphics interface vtable pointer from g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c)\n4. Tail jump to draw handler at vtable offset 0x54\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwCurrentFrameIndex - Current rendering frame counter\n- IMPLICIT: g_pGfxInterface - Graphics interface vtable pointer\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwGameFlags - Receives previous frame index value\n\nReturns:\n- void (tail call to draw handler, return handled by callee)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x54: Offset of Draw method in graphics interface vtable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function uses tail call optimization (JMP instead of CALL+RET)\n- Frame index copied to g_dwGameFlags enables frame delta calculations",
