      "name": "GfxIsDisplayTypeAccelerated",
      "signature": "void GfxIsDisplayTypeAccelerated(dword nUnused1, dword nUnused2, dword nValue1, dword nValue2, dword nValue3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Calls graphics interface function after validating mode and toggle state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate g_nVideoMode >= 4\n2. Validate g_fSomeToggle != 0\n3. Call graphics interface (g_pGfxInterface + 0x64) with 3 parameters\n\nParameters:\n- nUnused1: Unused parameter (always passed but never referenced)\n- nUnused2: Unused parameter (always passed but never referenced)\n- nValue1: Graphics parameter 1 (passed to interface)\n- nValue2: Graphics parameter 2 (passed to interface)\n- nValue3: Graphics parameter 3 (passed to interface)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value, assertions trigger on validation failures)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6faa51d9: Called on assertion failures\n- FogAssert: Graphics assertion macro",
