      "name": "GfxInterface_CallMethod0x68",
      "signature": "void GfxInterface_CallMethod0x68(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Graphics interface dispatch for vtable method at offset 0x68.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_nVideoMode and validate it equals 4, 5, 6, or 7 (accelerated display types)\n2. If invalid mode, assert with szAssertDisplayType at line 0x98 and exit(-1)\n3. Check g_dwExpansionModeToggle is non-zero (perspective/expansion initialized)\n4. If zero, assert with szAssertPerspective at line 0x99 and exit(-1)\n5. Load 3 parameters from stack (dwParam1, dwParam2, dwParam3) at offsets +0x10, +0x14, +0x18\n6. Load g_pGfxInterface vtable pointer\n7. Call vtable method at offset 0x68 with arguments (0, dwParam1, dwParam2, dwParam3)\n8. Clean 0x18 bytes (6 dwords) from stack via __stdcall RET\n\nParameters:\n- 6 stack parameters total, only 3 are used (dwParam1-3), first 3 appear unused\n- dwParam1 (uint): First graphics parameter passed to vtable method\n- dwParam2 (uint): Second graphics parameter passed to vtable method  \n- dwParam3 (uint): Third graphics parameter passed to vtable method\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Video modes 4-7 represent accelerated (hardware) graphics modes\n- Video modes less than 4 are software rendering and not supported by this function\n- Expansion mode toggle must be set before calling graphics interface methods\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x68: Vtable offset for graphics interface method\n- 0x98 (152): Assert line number for display type check\n- 0x99 (153): Assert line number for perspective check\n- 0x18: Stack cleanup size (6 dwords)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GfxInterface_CallMethod0x64: Similar dispatch at vtable offset 0x64\n- GfxInterface_CallMethod0x6C: Similar dispatch at vtable offset 0x6c\n- FogAssert: Debug assertion macro\n- Exit: Process termination on assertion failure",
