      "comment": "Validates graphics system state and invokes display interface method 0x6C.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load video mode from g_nVideoMode global\n2. Validate video mode is one of the 4 valid display types:\n   - 4: DISPLAYTYPE_GLIDE\n   - 5: DISPLAYTYPE_DIRECT3D\n   - 6: DISPLAYTYPE_RAVE\n   - 7: DISPLAYTYPE_SOFTWARE\n3. If invalid video mode, assert with \"gtGfxSystem.eDispType == DISPLAYTYPE_*\" message\n   and call Exit(-1) to terminate\n4. Check g_dwExpansionModeToggle is non-zero (perspective/expansion initialized)\n5. If zero, assert with \"gtGfxOptions.fPerspective\" message and Exit(-1)\n6. Load g_pGfxInterface vtable pointer and jump to method at offset 0x6C (method 27)\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- void (tail call to interface method)\n\nClassification: Public API / Wrapper\n- Exported ordinal function wrapping graphics interface call\n- Validates state before delegating to vtable method\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4: DISPLAYTYPE_GLIDE\n- 0x5: DISPLAYTYPE_DIRECT3D\n- 0x6: DISPLAYTYPE_RAVE\n- 0x7: DISPLAYTYPE_SOFTWARE\n- 0xa8 (168): Assert line for display type validation\n- 0xa9 (169): Assert line for perspective validation\n- 0x6c (108): Vtable offset for interface method 27\n\nGlobal State Accessed:\n- g_nVideoMode (0x6fabd228): Current video display type\n- g_dwExpansionModeToggle (0x6faae190): Expansion/perspective mode flag\n- g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c): Graphics interface vtable pointer\n\nError Handling:\n- Invalid video mode: FogAssert at Scale.cpp:168, then Exit(-1)\n- Expansion mode not set: FogAssert at Scale.cpp:169, then Exit(-1)\n\nSource: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Gfx\\SRC\\Scale.cpp",
