      "name": "GfxInterface_CallMethod0x88",
      "signature": "void GfxInterface_CallMethod0x88(uint dwParam1, uint dwParam2, uint dwParam3, uint dwParam4, uint dwParam5, uint dwParam6)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Thunk for graphics interface method at offset 0x88.\n\nForwards all 6 parameters to a virtual method on the graphics interface object (g_pGfxInterface).\nThis is an exported ordinal (10073) providing external access to internal graphics functionality.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pGfxInterface pointer from global\n2. Reorder and push all 6 parameters for virtual call\n3. Call virtual method at vtable offset 0x88\n4. Return (callee cleans stack via __stdcall)\n\nParameters:\n  dwParam1 - First parameter forwarded to interface method\n  dwParam2 - Second parameter forwarded to interface method\n  dwParam3 - Third parameter forwarded to interface method\n  dwParam4 - Fourth parameter forwarded to interface method\n  dwParam5 - Fifth parameter forwarded to interface method\n  dwParam6 - Sixth parameter forwarded to interface method\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nCalling Convention: __stdcall (callee cleans 24 bytes from stack via RET 0x18)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  GfxInterfaceCall84 - Similar thunk for method 0x84\n  GfxInterface_CallMethod0x5C - Similar thunk for method 0x5C\n  GfxInterface_CallMethod0x4C - Similar thunk for method 0x4C\n\nGlobal Data:\n  g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c) - Pointer to graphics interface vtable",
