      "comment": "Conditional graphics interface draw wrapper - calls graphics rendering function only if mode is enabled.\n\nOrdinal: 10074\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load nMode parameter from stack [ESP + 0x14]\n2. Test if nMode is zero (disabled)\n3. If nMode == 0, skip to return (no drawing)\n4. Load dwColor, dwY, dwX parameters from stack\n5. Load g_pGfxInterface pointer from global 0x6fabd21c\n6. Call virtual function at vtable offset 0x8c with (dwX, dwY, nMode, dwColor)\n7. Return, cleaning 24 bytes from stack (6 DWORD params)\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnused1 (uint): Unused parameter (not passed to vtable call)\n- dwUnused2 (uint): Unused parameter (not passed to vtable call)\n- dwX (uint): X coordinate for drawing operation\n- dwY (uint): Y coordinate for drawing operation\n- nMode (int): Rendering mode flag - if 0, drawing is skipped entirely\n- dwColor (uint): Color value for rendering (ARGB format)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nCalling Convention: __stdcall (callee cleans 24 bytes via RET 0x18)\n\nGlobal Data:\n- g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c): Pointer to graphics interface vtable\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GfxInterface_CallMethod0x88 (Ordinal_10073): Unconditional version at offset 0x88\n- GfxInterfaceCall84: Similar thunk for method 0x84\n\nNotes:\n- Virtual function dispatch through g_pGfxInterface pointer table\n- The conditional check allows callers to disable drawing by passing nMode=0\n- Only 4 of the 6 parameters are forwarded to the underlying vtable method",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
