      "name": "GfxInterface_CallMethod0x94",
      "signature": "void GfxInterface_CallMethod0x94(uint dwUnused1, uint dwUnused2, uint dwArg1, uint dwArg2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Invokes graphics interface method at vtable offset 0x94.\n\nThunk/Wrapper function that forwards 4 arguments to the graphics interface\nvtable method at offset 0x94 (148 bytes). The first two parameters appear\nunused by the caller pattern (always 0 or ignored).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load dwArg2 from stack [ESP+0x10] into EAX\n2. Load dwArg1 from stack [ESP+0xc] into ECX  \n3. Load dwUnused2 from stack [ESP+0x8] into EDX\n4. Push dwArg2 (EAX) as 4th argument\n5. Load g_pGfxInterface vtable pointer from global\n6. Push dwArg1 (ECX) as 3rd argument\n7. Load dwUnused1 from stack [ESP+0xc] (adjusted) into ECX\n8. Call vtable method at offset 0x94 with 4 arguments\n9. Return to caller (stdcall cleans 16 bytes)\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnused1 (uint) - First parameter, passed through but typically unused\n  dwUnused2 (uint) - Second parameter, passed through but typically unused\n  dwArg1 (uint) - Third parameter, passed to vtable method\n  dwArg2 (uint) - Fourth parameter, passed to vtable method\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value (vtable method return ignored)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_pGfxInterface is NULL, will crash (no null check)\n  - Vtable offset 0x94 = 148 decimal = method index 37 (4-byte pointers)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - GfxInterface_CallMethod0x5C (similar thunk at offset 0x5C)\n  - GfxInterface_CallMethod0x4C (similar thunk at offset 0x4C)\n  - GfxInterface_CallMethod0xA8 (similar thunk at offset 0xA8)",
