      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "GfxInterface_CallMethod0x9C - Graphics interface vtable wrapper\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load dwParam3, dwParam2, dwParam1 from stack positions 0x14, 0x10, 0x0c\n2. Push parameters in reverse order (dwParam3, dwParam2, dwParam1)\n3. Load g_pGfxInterface global pointer from 0x6fabd21c\n4. Call function pointer at vtable offset 0x9c: [g_pGfxInterface + 0x9c]\n5. Clean up 5 stack parameters (0x14 bytes) via RET 0x14\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnused1 (uint): Reserved/unused - passed for ABI compatibility\n- dwUnused2 (uint): Reserved/unused - passed for ABI compatibility  \n- dwParam1 (uint): First parameter forwarded to GfxInterface method\n- dwParam2 (uint): Second parameter forwarded to GfxInterface method\n- dwParam3 (uint): Third parameter forwarded to GfxInterface method\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nClassification:\n- Thunk/Wrapper function - forwards 3 of 5 params to vtable method\n- Exported function (export ordinal 10080) for external callers\n\nCalled From:\n- Export table entry at 0x6faad1d8\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n- g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c): Graphics interface vtable pointer",
