      "name": "GfxInterface_DrawRectangle",
      "signature": "void GfxInterface_DrawRectangle(dword dwUnused1, dword dwUnused2, dword nX, dword nY, dword nWidth, dword nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Graphics interface method dispatcher - invokes virtual function at offset 0xa0 of g_pGfxInterface.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load parameters 3-6 into registers (EDX, ECX, EAX)\n2. Push parameters 3-6 onto stack (right-to-left for __stdcall)\n3. Load g_pGfxInterface pointer into EAX\n4. Call virtual method at offset 0xa0\n5. Return with stack cleanup (RET 0x18 cleans 6 parameters)\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnused1: Unused parameter (may be reserved)\n- dwUnused2: Unused parameter (may be reserved)\n- nX: X coordinate for graphics operation\n- nY: Y coordinate for graphics operation\n- nWidth: Width value for graphics operation\n- nHeight: Height value for graphics operation\n\nReturns:\n- void (result of virtual method is discarded)\n\nNotes:\n- This is a wrapper that delegates to the active graphics implementation\n- Parameters 1-2 are loaded but not used in the virtual method call\n- Virtual function offset 0xa0 likely implements DrawRectangle or similar graphics primitive",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a71d9a20621570141f5127f7a25c0932",
