      "name": "SetGlobalVisibilityState",
      "signature": "void SetGlobalVisibilityState(uint dwValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Sets the global window visibility target state.\n\nClassification: Public API (exported ordinal setter)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load dwValue parameter from stack (ESP+4)\n2. Store value to global g_dwGlobalState at 0x6fabd810\n3. Return to caller (stdcall: RET 4 cleans stack)\n\nParameters:\n- dwValue (uint): Target visibility state (0=hidden, non-zero=visible)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetVisibilityState: Reads this value and applies visibility transitions\n- The stored value is checked against g_dwCurrentVisibilityState before any state transition\n\nMemory Model:\n- Writes to global g_dwGlobalState (0x6fabd810)\n- No allocation or ownership semantics\n- Value persists until next call\n\nCross-Reference:\n- Exported as Ordinal 10025\n- Referenced by data at 0x6faad0fc (export table)",
