      "name": "VsprintfFuncFormatter",
      "signature": "int VsprintfFuncFormatter(void * pContext, byte * pbFormat)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Formats and outputs a format string with variable arguments using callback handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize context state with maximum width of 0x7fffffff\n2. Invoke FUN_6faa6105 to parse format string and generate formatted output\n3. Decrement the width counter by 1 after formatting\n4. Check if width counter is negative (error condition)\n5. If negative, call FUN_6faa5fed for error cleanup and finalization\n6. If non-negative, null-terminate the output buffer at context location\n7. Return the formatted result from callback function\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (void*): Output context structure passed to formatter callbacks\n- pbFormat (byte*): Format string to parse and format\n\nReturns:\n- Return value from FUN_6faa6105 formatter (typically character count)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
