      "name": "SehUnwindHandler",
      "signature": "void SehUnwindHandler(void * pTargetFrame, PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "SEH unwinder that restores exception context during structured exception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current ExceptionList pointer to local variable\n2. Call RtlUnwind with target frame, return address, exception record, and zero value\n3. Clear EXCEPTION_UNWINDING flag (0x2) from ExceptionFlags in the exception record\n4. Restore the saved ExceptionList pointer by dereferencing saved pointer\n5. Store original ExceptionList back into restored exception frame\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pTargetFrame (void*): Target exception frame for stack unwinding; RtlUnwind will unwind to this frame\n- pExceptionRecord (PEXCEPTION_RECORD): Exception record containing flags and exception info\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value; called for side effects only)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- RtlUnwind (kernel32.dll): Performs actual stack unwinding\n- SehDispatcher: Calls this handler during exception dispatch",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:50b3897ed620463feed31471327a96ee",
