      "name": "FindRangeEntryIndex",
      "signature": "int * FindRangeEntryIndex(void * pTable, int nIterations, int nValue, uint * pdwFoundIndex, uint * pdwFoundOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Finds a range entry matching a given value using binary search pattern.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load table header: entry count at offset +0xc, array base at +0x10\n2. Initialize index to starting count, iterate through nIterations times\n3. Each iteration decrements index and compares nValue against range bounds\n4. Range test checks if nValue in [entry.min, entry.max] at 20-byte strides\n5. On match, stores current and previous indices in output parameters\n6. Validates result indices are within table bounds before returning\n\nParameters:\n- pTable (void*): Table structure with metadata and range array\n- nIterations (int): Number of search iterations to perform\n- nValue (int): Value to find within a range entry\n- pdwFoundIndex (uint*): Output - index of matching range entry\n- pdwFoundOffset (uint*): Output - previous index from search iteration\n\nReturns:\n- int*: Pointer to matching entry's data block (base + index * 0x14)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc: Offset to entry count in table header\n- 0x10: Offset to array base in table header\n- 0x14 (20): Stride between range entries\n- 0x4, 0x8: Range min/max field offsets within entry",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:aeb6015352f39d3219cf32b63d44a754",
