      "name": "ReallocateMemoryWithRetry",
      "signature": "void * ReallocateMemoryWithRetry(void * param1, void * param2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Reallocates memory buffer with configurable retry behavior.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pbBuffer is NULL, allocate new memory of requested size\n2. If pdwSize is NULL, free buffer and return NULL\n3. Otherwise, attempt reallocation with retry loop:\n   - Check allocation mode (DAT_6fabee24: 3=locked section, 2=cache-based, other=standard)\n   - For locked sections: acquire section lock, validate size bounds, copy data\n   - For cache-based: retrieve cache entry, validate cache size, copy data\n   - For standard: round size to 16-byte alignment, use HeapReAlloc\n   - On allocation failure, call FUN_6faa9188 retry handler in loop\n\nParameters:\n- pbBuffer (byte*): Existing buffer to reallocate, or NULL to allocate new\n- pdwSize (uint*): Requested size in bytes, or NULL to free buffer\n- IMPLICIT: DAT_6fabee24 controls allocation strategy\n- IMPLICIT: DAT_6fabee20 is heap handle\n- IMPLICIT: ExceptionList for exception handling chain\n\nReturns:\n- byte*: Reallocated/allocated buffer on success\n- NULL: On failure or if pbSize is NULL with non-NULL pbBuffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xffffffe1 (size limit): Maximum allocation size check\n- 0xfU & 0xfffffff0: Rounds size to 16-byte alignment\n- 0x1, 0x10 (0x10000): Default/minimum allocation sizes\n- 0x80000000 (-1): Exception marker in local_8",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:da9fe63256c776da60d8a55e82f34c74",
