      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Returns the allocated size of a heap block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check allocation mode (3 or 2) and initialize exception handler\n2. If mode 3: Call FUN_6faa7fbc to get buffer, compute size from header\n3. If mode 2: Call FUN_6faa8d17 to get buffer and flags, compute size from buffer\n4. If mode neither 3 nor 2: Call HeapSize API directly\n5. Restore exception handler and return size\n\nParameters:\n- pBlock (void*): Pointer to allocated heap block\n\nReturns:\n- SIZE_T: Size of the allocated block in bytes",
