      "name": "AllocateMemoryWithMode",
      "signature": "void AllocateMemoryWithMode(uint * pnSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates memory using one of three allocation strategies based on g_nAllocationMode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If mode is 3: Allocate from protected pool if size <= g_dwMaxBufSize\n2. If mode is 2: Round up size to 16-byte boundary, allocate from cache if <= g_dwCacheLimit\n3. Otherwise: Round up size and allocate from process heap via HeapAlloc\n\nParameters:\n- pnSize (uint*): Requested allocation size in bytes (pointer to size value)\n\nReturns:\n- void (allocation status handled via exception handlers)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0F (15): Mask for 16-byte boundary alignment\n- 0xFFFFFFF0: Alignment mask for 16-byte rounding\n- 0x10 (16): Minimum allocation size and alignment quantum",
