      "name": "FormatStringParser",
      "signature": "int FormatStringParser(int * pOutput, byte * pFormatStr, undefined4 * pArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Parses printf-style format string and outputs formatted result.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read format string character by character\n2. Process format specifiers (% codes) to determine output formatting\n3. Parse format flags (space, +, -, 0, #), width, precision, and size modifiers\n4. Retrieve arguments based on type specifiers (d, u, x, X, o, c, s, p, f, e, g, n)\n5. Convert arguments to strings using appropriate radix/floating point conversion\n6. Apply width and precision constraints with padding/sign handling\n7. Write formatted output via FUN_6faa68ac callback\n8. Continue until null terminator or error encountered\n\nParameters:\n- pOutput (int *): Output buffer or stream handle passed to write callbacks\n- pFormatStr (byte *): Null-terminated format string (ASCII)\n- pArgs (undefined4 *): Pointer to variadic arguments array\n\nReturns:\n- Number of characters written (nCharsWritten) on success\n- Negative value on error (e.g., invalid encoding in wide-char conversion)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Space character (flag 2)\n- 0x23 (35): Hash character (flag 0x80 for alternate form)\n- 0x2b (43): Plus sign (flag 1 for sign+)\n- 0x2d (45): Minus sign (flag 4 for left-align)\n- 0x30 (48): Zero character (flag 8 for zero-pad)\n- 0x80, 0x100, 0x200, etc.: Formatting flags (sign, alternate, zero-pad, left-align)\n- 0x810: Wide-char flag combination\n- 0x8000: 64-bit integer flag (I64 modifier)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:b7a52aed3655c7d65807498f610c8ff8",
