      "name": "BufferCharacterToStream",
      "signature": "void BufferCharacterToStream(uint dwChar, int * piStream, int * pnCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Buffers a character to output stream or flushes when buffer is full.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment buffer position counter at offset +1\n2. Decrement remaining buffer space\n3. Test if buffer has room (position >= 0)\n4. If buffer full, call FormatCharacterToStream to flush and retry\n5. If buffer has space, write character byte to buffer\n6. Increment buffer pointer and mask to low byte (0xFF)\n7. On success, increment output count\n8. On flush failure, set count to -1 (error indicator)\n\nParameters:\n- dwChar (uint): Character code to buffer (uses low byte 0xFF)\n- piStream (int*): Pointer to stream structure (FILE-like)\n  Contains buffer state, position counter, and stream flags\n- pnCount (int*): Pointer to output character count\n  Incremented on success, set to -1 on flush failure\n\nReturns:\n- void (success/failure indicated via pnCount: incremented on success, -1 on failure)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:48de6fa61a4bf40c36c288aa452eb3ad",
