      "name": "GetExceptionHandlerContext",
      "signature": "dword * GetExceptionHandlerContext(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Gets or initializes the thread-local exception handler context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current last error code and save it\n2. Retrieve TLS value from thread-local storage index\n3. If TLS is NULL, allocate new handler context (0x74 bytes)\n4. Set TLS to new context and initialize handler fields\n5. Store current thread ID and sentinel value in context\n6. Restore original last error code before returning\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwThreadLocalStorageIndex (global TLS index)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to handler context (DWORD *) with thread ID at offset 0, sentinel at offset 4\n- Returns NULL on allocation failure (calls __amsg_exit)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeHandlerFields: Initializes handler context structure\n- ProcessExceptionInfo: Uses returned context for exception dispatching",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6dad5d06763847d66c3aa4a89105e250",
