      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize stream descriptors from startup info and standard handles.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate initial stream descriptor table (0x480 bytes)\n2. Initialize all entries with invalid handle (0xffffffff)\n3. Retrieve startup info to check for inherited stream handles\n4. Process inherited streams from startup info if available\n5. For uninitialized streams, retrieve standard I/O handles (stdin, stdout, stderr)\n6. Query file type for each handle and set appropriate flags\n7. Call SetHandleCount to finalize handle table\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_apStreamPointers array storage\n- IMPLICIT: g_nStreamCount stream limit (0x20 initially)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x480 (1152): Stream descriptor table size\n- 0x120 (288): Table entries per allocation (stream record size 0x24 = 36 bytes)\n- 0x7ff (2047): Maximum inherited stream count limit\n- 0x800 (2048): Clamped stream count\n- 0xfffffff6, 0xfffffff5, 0xfffffff4: STD_INPUT/OUTPUT/ERROR handles\n- 0x81, 0x80, 0x40: Stream flags for handle type/origin",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
