      "name": "CleanupStreamDescriptors",
      "signature": "void CleanupStreamDescriptors(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleanup stream descriptor resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through g_apStreamDescriptors array\n2. For each non-null descriptor:\n   a. Iterate through descriptor entries (stride 0x24 bytes)\n   b. Check if SpinCount field (!= 0) at offset -0x4\n   c. If present, call DeleteCriticalSection on CRITICAL_SECTION at offset 0xc\n3. Call FUN_6faa7e03 to deallocate descriptor memory\n4. Clear descriptor pointer\n\nParameters:\n- Implicit: Iterates from g_apStreamDescriptors (0x6fabee40) to 0x6fabef40 (4 entries)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x480 (1152): Total descriptor size\n- 0x24 (36): Entry stride size (matches CRITICAL_SECTION layout)\n- 0xc (12): Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION in descriptor entry\n- 0x4: Offset to SpinCount field relative to CRITICAL_SECTION pointer\n- 0x6fabef40: End boundary for iteration",
