      "comment": "Allocate and initialize resource data buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if module path is cached; if not, call initialization routine\n2. Get current module filename into cache buffer\n3. Determine actual path: use default module path or override from config\n4. Calculate required buffer size by calling resource parser\n5. Allocate heap buffer for resource data\n6. Populate resource buffer via second parse pass\n7. Store buffer pointer and final data count to globals\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: Uses module path from DAT_6fabef44 (override) or default\n\nReturns:\n- void; Sets globals: DAT_6fabd864 (buffer pointer), DAT_6fabd860 (data count)",
