      "name": "ParseCommandLineArguments",
      "signature": "void ParseCommandLineArguments(byte * pbInputString, uint * pdwTokenPtrs, byte * pbOutputBuffer, uint * pnTokenCount, uint * pnOutputLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Parses a command-line string into tokens, handling quoted strings and escape sequences.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Process initial quoted string (if starts with 0x22 '\"')\n2. Handle escape sequences (0x5c '\\') based on character table at DAT_6fabdce0\n3. Parse unquoted arguments separated by spaces or tabs\n4. Support quote toggling within arguments for embedded quoted sections\n5. Track output length and token count\n6. Store token pointers and null-terminated parsed output\n\nParameters:\n- pbInputString: Input command-line string to parse\n- pdwTokenPtrs: Array to store pointers to parsed tokens (null-terminated)\n- pbOutputBuffer: Output buffer for parsed string (may be null for length-only)\n- pnTokenCount: Pointer to token counter (incremented for each token)\n- pnOutputLength: Pointer to output length counter\n\nReturns:\n- void (results via output parameters)\n\nNotes:\n- DAT_6fabdce0 is character classification table (bit 2 = special char)\n- Processes 0x20 (space), 0x09 (tab), 0x5c (\\), 0x22 (\") specially\n- Handles escaped quotes in quoted strings",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
