      "name": "GetEnvironmentStringsAsAnsi",
      "signature": "char * GetEnvironmentStringsAsAnsi(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves environment variable strings in ANSI/ASCII format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_nEnvironmentStringMode state: 0=uninitialized, 1=Unicode cached, 2=ANSI cached\n2. If mode=0 (first call), try GetEnvironmentStringsW() for Unicode version\n3. If successful, set mode=1 and convert wide-char strings to ANSI using WideCharToMultiByte()\n4. If Unicode unavailable or fails, fall back to GetEnvironmentStringsA() and set mode=2\n5. Return cached ANSI environment strings, allocated via _malloc()\n\nParameters:\n- (void): No parameters\n\nReturns:\n- LPSTR: Pointer to ANSI environment strings block (must be freed by caller via FreeEnvironmentStringsA)\n- NULL: If environment string retrieval fails\n\nNotes:\n- Uses static g_nEnvironmentStringMode to cache the OS capabilities (Unicode vs ANSI)\n- Allocates memory for wide-to-ANSI conversion; caller must free returned pointer\n- Environment strings are null-terminated pairs: VAR1=val1\\0VAR2=val2\\0\\0",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
