      "name": "GetMsvcrtHeapSelection",
      "signature": "int GetMsvcrtHeapSelection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Determines MSVC runtime heap selection based on Windows version and environment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6faaa660() for initialization\n2. Get Windows version info with GetVersionExA\n3. Check if Windows version is Vista+ (MajorVersion == 6, MinorVersion >= 5)\n4. If pre-Vista: get __MSVCRT_HEAP_SELECT environment variable\n5. If set, parse heap specification and extract heap ID with FUN_6faaa2b4\n6. Call ExtractPEVersionInfo for legacy version detection\n7. Return heap selection (1=low, 2=reserved, 3=custom)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: No explicit parameters; operates on runtime environment\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Standard heap\n- 2: Reserved/special heap\n- 3: Custom heap or extraction failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
