      "name": "CleanupGameMemory",
      "signature": "void CleanupGameMemory(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Deallocates game memory based on allocation mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If allocation mode is 3: Loop through DAT_6fabee14 allocation blocks, each 20 bytes apart (stride 5 dwords)\n   - Free virtual memory region at offset 0xc with 0x100000 size\n   - Free committed virtual memory\n   - Free heap memory at offset 0x1c (puVar1[1])\n2. Else if allocation mode is 2: Follow circular linked list at PTR_LOOP_6faae900\n   - For each node, free virtual memory if pointer at offset 0x10 is non-NULL\n   - Advance to next node via pointer at offset 0\n3. Finally destroy process heap (terminates allocation system)\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global allocation mode and handles)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc (12): Offset to first virtual memory pointer in allocation block\n- 0x1c (28): Offset to heap allocation in allocation block\n- 0x100000 (1048576): Virtual memory region size\n- 0x4000: MEM_DECOMMIT flag\n- 0x8000: MEM_RELEASE flag\n- 0x10: Offset to memory pointer in linked list node",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
