      "name": "CxxFrameHandler3",
      "signature": "void CxxFrameHandler3(PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExcRecord, PVOID pContext, DWORD dwMode, uint dwEstablisherFrame, int * pDispatcher, int nHandlerReturn, PVOID pDispatcherContext, byte bFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "C++ exception handler for structured exception handling dispatcher.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate magic number (0x19930520) in dispatcher\n2. Check ExceptionFlags for continuation bit (0x66)\n3. If handler not yet invoked (param_5[3] != 0):\n   - Verify exception code matches C++ thrown object (0xe06d7363)\n   - Validate exception info parameter count\n   - Call registered handler via function pointer at ExceptionInformation[2]+8\n4. If exception is continuation and cleanup handler exists:\n   - Invoke cleanup handler via FUN_6faa783e\n5. Return status (1 for handled, 0 for continue)\n\nParameters:\n- pExcRecord (PEXCEPTION_RECORD): Exception record with code and info\n- pContext (PVOID): CPU context at exception point\n- dwMode (DWORD): Nested exception level\n- dwEstablisherFrame (uint): Establisher frame pointer\n- pDispatcher (int*): Dispatcher context [0]=magic, [1]=cleanup flags, [3]=invoke flag\n- nHandlerReturn (int): Handler return value\n- pDispatcherContext (PVOID): Additional dispatcher context\n- byFlags (char): Handler flags\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on successful handling\n- 0 to continue search or propagate exception\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CxxFrameHandler: Main dispatcher\n- SehExceptionFilter: Filter routine\n- RaiseException: Exception raiser",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
