      "name": "ProcessSEHException",
      "signature": "void ProcessSEHException(PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord, PVOID pContext, DWORD dwContextSize, uint dwUnknown, uint dwHandlerTable, char cTerminate, int nRangeIndex, PVOID pDispatcher)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Processes Structured Exception Handling (SEH) exceptions for range-based handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate exception offset against handler table bounds\n2. Check for C++ typed exception signature (0xe06d7363)\n3. If C++ exception detected, extract exception info from handler context\n4. Search handler ranges for matching exception offset\n5. For each matching range, iterate through handlers with their vtables\n6. Attempt to match exception with each handler vtable entry\n7. On match, invoke handler with exception and context information\n8. On mismatch or unhandled, escalate to next handler or terminate\n\nParameters:\n- pExceptionRecord (PEXCEPTION_RECORD): Exception information (code, params)\n- pContext (PVOID): Execution context pointer\n- dwContextSize (DWORD): Size of context structure\n- dwUnknown (uint): Unknown parameter (reserved/flags)\n- dwHandlerTable (uint): Base address of exception handler table\n- cTerminate (char): Termination flag (0=continue, non-zero=terminate)\n- nRangeIndex (int): Current range/frame index\n- pDispatcher (PVOID): Dispatcher context pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void (control flow determined by exception handling result)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xe06d7363: C++ typed exception signature\n- 0x19930520: C++ exception magic cookie\n- 0x1b, 0x1c: Handler context offsets in exception handler context\n- 0xc, 0x10: Vtable and handler offsets in exception information",
