      "name": "ProcessRangeExceptionHandlers",
      "signature": "void ProcessRangeExceptionHandlers(PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord, PVOID pContext, DWORD dwContextSize, dword dwUnknown, uint dwHandlerTable, int nExceptionOffset, int nRangeIndex, PVOID pDispatcher)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Processes exception handlers within ranges for structured exception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get exception handler context to check for pending C++ exceptions\n2. Skip processing if handler context indicates exception was already handled\n3. Find matching range entry for the exception offset using binary search\n4. For each matching range, iterate through vtable entries\n5. Check if handler matches exception type signature\n6. If match found, invoke FUN_6faa78f2 to execute handler\n7. Continue to next range entry until all ranges processed\n\nParameters:\n- pExceptionRecord (PEXCEPTION_RECORD): Exception info (code, params)\n- pContext (PVOID): Execution context pointer\n- dwContextSize (DWORD): Size of context structure\n- dwUnknown (dword): Unknown/reserved parameter\n- dwHandlerTable (uint): Base address of handler table\n- nExceptionOffset (int): Exception offset to match against ranges\n- nRangeIndex (int): Current frame/range index\n- pDispatcher (PVOID): Dispatcher context pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void (control flow determined by handler execution)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1a: Offset to handler context pending flag\n- 0x10: Stride of vtable entry in handler table\n- -0xc: Offset to handler vtable pointer\n- -0x10: Offset to handler base address",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
