      "name": "ProcessExceptionFrames",
      "signature": "void ProcessExceptionFrames(FrameNode * pFrameNode, uint dwFrameInfo, FrameIterator * pIterator, int nTargetNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Iterates linked list of exception frames, invoking handler for each.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH frame registration with exception handler\n2. Load starting frame index from pFrameNode->nCurrentFrame\n3. Loop while current frame index != nTargetNode:\n   a. Validate frame index is within bounds [0, pIterator->nFrameCount)\n   b. Call FUN_6faa7dad on bounds violation (error path)\n   c. Retrieve handler callback from pIterator->pFrameTable[index]\n   d. If handler exists, invoke __CallSettingFrame with flag 0x103\n   e. Advance to next frame via pIterator->pFrameTable[index].next\n4. Write final frame index back to pFrameNode->nCurrentFrame\n5. Restore exception handler state\n\nParameters:\n- pFrameNode (FrameNode*): Frame node with current index at offset +8\n- dwFrameInfo (uint): Handler invocation flag (0x103 = frame setup)\n- pIterator (FrameIterator*): Frame descriptor with bounds and handler table\n- nTargetNode (int): Target frame index to stop iteration\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x103: Frame info flag passed to handler\n- 0x8: Offset of frame index in FrameNode\n- 0x4: Offset of frame count in FrameIterator  \n- 0x8: Offset of frame table in FrameIterator\n- 0x8: Stride of frame entries (2 dwords each)",
