      "name": "SehHandlerStep",
      "signature": "void SehHandlerStep(PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExcRecord, PVOID pCurrentFrame, DWORD dwFlags, uint dwUnknown, int nHandlerIndex, byte * pbFrameInfo, byte * pbDispatchInfo, int * pnState, int nStateDelta, PVOID pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Process a single SEH handler step during exception unwinding and dispatch.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If dispatch info provided, validate/prepare it via helper function\n2. Set context to current frame if no context override provided\n3. Unwind the handler stack to prepare for handler execution\n4. Update frame state counter by incrementing with nStateDelta\n5. Locate appropriate handler from exception record metadata\n6. If handler found, execute dispatcher to invoke handler code\n\nParameters:\n- pExcRecord (PEXCEPTION_RECORD): Exception record descriptor\n- pCurrentFrame (PVOID): Current stack frame pointer\n- dwFlags (DWORD): Control flags (reserved for future use)\n- dwUnknown (uint): Unknown parameter encoding\n- nHandlerIndex (int): Index within handler table\n- pbFrameInfo (byte*): Pointer to frame information\n- pbDispatchInfo (byte*): Pointer to dispatch/unwind data\n- pnState (int*): Pointer to state counter\n- nStateDelta (int): State increment value\n- pContext (PVOID): Optional context override\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)",
