      "name": "ProcessAllocatedMemory",
      "signature": "void ProcessAllocatedMemory(void * pMemory)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Process and clean up allocated memory based on allocation mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if memory pointer is valid\n2. Based on g_nAllocationMode, invoke appropriate cleanup:\n   - Mode 3: Call FUN_6faa7fbc to retrieve allocation info, then FUN_6faa7fe7 to cleanup\n   - Mode 2: Call FUN_6faa8d17 to get allocation params, then FUN_6faa8d6e to cleanup\n3. If result is NULL, fallback to HeapFree for direct deallocation\n4. Restore exception handler on exit\n\nParameters:\n- pMemory (void*): Pointer to allocated memory block to process\n\nReturns:\n- void (implicit result status in local_8: 0=success, -1=unprocessed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3: Allocation mode for type 3 processing\n- 0x2: Allocation mode for type 2 processing\n- 0x9: Critical section identifier",
