      "name": "FindAllocBlockByAddress",
      "signature": "void * FindAllocBlockByAddress(int nMemAddress)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Searches allocation block table for block containing given memory address.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer to start of allocation block table\n2. Loop through blocks with stride 0x14 (20 bytes)\n3. Check if table boundary exceeded (end of blocks)\n4. Compare memory address against block's base (stored at offset 0xc)\n5. If address is within 0x100000 bytes of block base, return block pointer\n6. Otherwise advance to next block and repeat\n7. If no block found, return NULL\n\nParameters:\n- nMemAddress (int): Memory address to search for in allocation blocks\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocation block structure containing address, or NULL if not found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): Size of allocation block structure entry\n- 0xc (12): Offset to base address field within block structure\n- 0x100000 (1048576): Maximum offset from block base to still be considered within block",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2a0dd1f395da0f8e13609d337843c676",
