      "name": "FreeAllocatedBlock",
      "signature": "void FreeAllocatedBlock(uint * pdwBlockTable, int nBlockOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Removes an allocated memory block from linked list and frees virtual/heap memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate block structure (check lower bit flags, refcount)\n2. If block is linked, unlink from doubly-linked list and update bitmap\n3. Merge adjacent blocks if valid, update size tracking\n4. When last block in bucket is freed, deallocate bucket virtual memory\n5. Update global allocation block table and counts\n\nParameters:\n- pdwBlockTable (uint *): Pointer to allocation block table\n- nBlockOffset (int): Byte offset to block within table\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies global state: DAT_6fabee10, DAT_6fabee08, DAT_6fabee0c, g_dwAllocBlockCount)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x204: Size of bucket/index table entry\n- 0x144, 0x44, 0xc4: Offsets to bitmap fields\n- 0x8000: Virtual memory page size\n- 0x1f, 0x20: Bit manipulation masks (32-bit boundaries)\n- 0x3f: Maximum bucket index (64 buckets)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ef5171f8f7487cff01081036951ae8fa",
