      "name": "AllocateMemoryBlock",
      "signature": "void * AllocateMemoryBlock(dword dwAllocationSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates a memory block of the specified size from the allocation table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align requested size to 16-byte boundary via (size + 0x17) & 0xfffffff0\n2. Calculate bit position from aligned size for bitmap lookup\n3. Build bitmasks for available slots based on size class\n4. Search allocation block table for block with contiguous free slots\n5. If no free slots found, allocate new block via FUN_6faa8619\n6. Find best-fit slot in selected block from available free list\n7. Remove allocated slot from free list by updating links\n8. Update block allocation bitmap to mark slot as used\n9. Initialize memory header with actual allocation size\n10. Return pointer to allocated memory\n\nParameters:\n- dwAllocationSize (dword): Number of bytes to allocate (will be aligned to 16-byte boundary)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated memory block on success\n- NULL on allocation failure (insufficient memory or unable to allocate new block)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ff64648b3e6e32bc28a5e4bc8d984c1e",
