      "name": "AllocateNewMemoryBlock",
      "signature": "dword * AllocateNewMemoryBlock(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new memory allocation block table entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if allocation block table is full (dwAllocBlockCount == dwAllocBlockSize)\n2. If full, reallocate table with 5x + 16 entries size using HeapReAlloc\n3. Create new allocation block structure at end of table\n4. Allocate 16.7KB heap memory for block metadata (0x41c4 bytes)\n5. Allocate 1MB virtual memory for block data (0x100000 bytes)\n6. Initialize block metadata: dwFlags=-1, nIndex=0, nNextFree=0\n7. Increment block count and initialize block's first free entry marker\n8. Return pointer to new block structure on success, NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global allocation state: g_hProcessHeap, g_dwAllocBlockCount, g_dwAllocBlockSize, g_pAllocBlockTable)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to new allocation block structure (array of 5 dwords) on success\n- NULL pointer on allocation failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5, 0x50: Allocation block structure size (5 dwords = 20 bytes)\n- 0x10: Block table growth increment\n- 0x41c4: Block metadata size (16.7KB)\n- 0x100000: Virtual allocation size per block (1MB)\n- 0x2000: MEM_RESERVE (virtual allocation flag)\n- 4: PAGE_READWRITE (protection flag)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b59a8a7d2c8fdcc2aac183f01f99a847",
