      "name": "AllocateMemoryPage",
      "signature": "int AllocateMemoryPage(int nContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates a 32KB memory page for the memory pool and initializes free list nodes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Count bits in pool's page allocation bitmask to find next page index\n2. Calculate page allocation table address based on pool context\n3. Initialize doubly-linked list nodes for the 0x40 free list entries\n4. Call VirtualAlloc to allocate 32KB (0x8000) page at calculated address\n5. If allocation succeeds, initialize free list chain for allocation granularity\n6. Link page into pool's data structure and update bitmask\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (int): Pool control structure address containing allocation params\n\nReturns:\n- Page index (0-based) on success\n- -1 on VirtualAlloc failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
