      "name": "ReallocateMemoryBlock",
      "signature": "int ReallocateMemoryBlock(uint * pdwMemMgr, int nOffset, int nSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Reallocates a memory block within managed pool, updating linked list and bitset tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate new block size (16-byte aligned) and memory bucket offset\n2. Validate sufficient remaining space in allocation source block\n3. If shrinking: unlink from current bucket, decrement refcount; insert into smaller bucket if needed\n4. If growing: unlink from current bucket, insert into larger bucket, manage bitset flags\n5. Update linked list pointers maintaining doubly-linked structure\n6. Update block header with new size\n7. Return 1 on success, 0 on validation failure\n\nParameters:\n- pdwMemMgr (uint *): Memory manager structure (offsets 0x44, 0xc4 for bitsets; 0x144 for bucket table)\n- nOffset (int): Offset within managed pool for allocation source block\n- nSize (int): Requested new block size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if reallocation successful\n- 0 if insufficient space or invalid parameters\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x17: Size alignment mask (24-byte minimum)\n- 0xfffffff0: Alignment to 16-byte boundary\n- 0x204: Bucket stride (516 bytes)\n- 0x144: Bucket table offset (324)\n- 0x3f: Maximum bucket index (63)\n- 0x1f: Bit shift mask (31)\n- 0x20: Bitset width for two-part flags (32-bit fields)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e4f799c77acab14c5b1bdda2181c2d46",
