      "comment": "Allocates and initializes the main game memory pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check memory pool mode flag (g_nMemoryPoolMode)\n2. If mode is -1, use static buffer PTR_LOOP_6faae900\n3. Otherwise, allocate heap memory of 0x2020 bytes via HeapAlloc\n4. Allocate virtual memory region of 0x400000 bytes for pool\n5. Commit initial 0x10000 bytes\n6. Link memory structures using doubly-linked list pointers\n7. Initialize 0x400 free list entries with size markers\n8. Set up 0x1000-byte page headers with link pointers\n9. Memset pool to zero, return memory pool handle\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global g_nMemoryPoolMode, g_hProcessHeap)\n\nReturns:\n- void**: Pointer to allocated memory pool structure on success\n- NULL: If any allocation fails (heap or virtual memory)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b10e654b1e0872dc227e39198444a376",
