      "name": "FindAllocationMetadata",
      "signature": "byte * FindAllocationMetadata(byte * pbMemory, dword * pdwMetadata, dword * pdwPageBase)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Locates allocation metadata node for a memory block in mode 2 allocator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Traverse linked list starting from PTR_LOOP_6faae900\n2. For each node, check if pbMemory falls within [node[4], node[5]) range\n3. When found, validate alignment (0xF) and minimum offset (0x100)\n4. Extract page base (0xFFF000 mask) and metadata pointer\n5. Return metadata pointer or NULL if not found\n\nParameters:\n- pbMemory (byte*): Pointer to allocated memory block to locate\n- pdwMetadata (dword*): Output - pointer to allocation metadata node\n- pdwPageBase (dword*): Output - page-aligned base address\n\nReturns:\n- byte*: Pointer to allocation metadata node, or NULL if not found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xF: Alignment requirement (16-byte boundary)\n- 0x100: Minimum offset from page boundary\n- 0xFFF000: Page alignment mask\n- 0xFFFFF000: Page base mask\n- 4, 8: Field offsets in allocation node structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
