      "name": "UpdateMemoryPageCounter",
      "signature": "void UpdateMemoryPageCounter(int * pPageBase, int nPageSize, byte * pbPageCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Updates the page counter for a memory page and triggers cleanup when limit reached.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate page entry address using base and size difference\n2. Add counter value to page counter, clear input byte\n3. Set page flag to 0xf1\n4. If page counter reaches 0xf0, increment free page count\n5. When free page count reaches 0x20 (32), free 16 pages\n\nParameters:\n- pPageBase (int*): Pointer to page table base\n- nPageSize (int): Current page size for offset calculation\n- pbPageCount (byte*): Pointer to page counter value to add\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, modifies memory state\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc: Right shift amount (4KB page granularity)\n- 0x8: Page entry size in bytes\n- 0x18: Offset to page array in structure\n- 0xf0: Page counter threshold\n- 0xf1: Page status flag\n- 0x10: Free operation parameter\n- 0x20: Cleanup trigger threshold",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
