      "name": "AllocateMemoryFromPool",
      "signature": "void * AllocateMemoryFromPool(dword dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates memory from a pooled memory manager.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search existing pools for free memory block of requested size\n2. If found, mark block as allocated and return pointer\n3. If not found, check for allocation pool with available slots\n4. If no pools available, allocate new pool from system via VirtualAlloc\n5. Initialize pool entries and return allocated block\n\nParameters:\n- dwSize (dword): Size of memory to allocate\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated memory block, or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x806: Pool entry count (2054 entries)\n- 0x1000 (4096): Page size / allocation unit\n- 0xf0 (240): Entry size in pool\n- 0x18: Pool header offset\n- 0x10: Pool descriptor offset\n- 0x100 (256): Returned block alignment offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
