      "name": "AllocateFromPool",
      "signature": "byte * AllocateFromPool(int * pPoolStruct, dword nBlockSize, dword nMarkerByte)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates a block of memory from a linked-list memory pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Scan the pool buffer for a free block marked by a zero byte\n2. Find the run length of zero bytes (consecutive zeros)\n3. If sufficient contiguous zeros exist, mark them with the marker byte\n4. Return a pointer to the allocated block\n\nParameters:\n- pPoolStruct (int*): Pool structure containing buffer pointer and allocation state at offsets 0 and 1, pool limit at offset 0x3e\n- nBlockSize (dword): Requested allocation size in bytes\n- nMarkerByte (dword): Marker byte to write to allocated blocks\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated block (with offset calculation: (pbResult * 0x10 + pPoolStruct * -0xf))\n- 0 if allocation fails (insufficient space or invalid parameters)",
