      "name": "TryHandleOutOfMemory",
      "signature": "int TryHandleOutOfMemory(uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Callback wrapper for out-of-memory event handler. Invokes registered callback and returns success status.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if callback function pointer is registered (g_pfnOutOfMemoryCallback != NULL)\n2. If registered, invoke callback with allocation size parameter\n3. Return 1 if callback succeeds (non-zero), 0 on failure or if no callback registered\n\nParameters:\n- dwSize (uint): Allocation size in bytes that triggered out-of-memory condition\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Callback succeeded or handled the allocation failure\n- 0: Callback failed or no callback was registered\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ReallocateMemoryWithRetry: Uses this function in retry loop for allocation failures\n- __nh_malloc: Uses this function in retry loop for allocation failures",
