      "name": "MoveMemory",
      "signature": "void * MoveMemory(void * pDest, void * pSrc, uint nLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Copies nLength bytes from pSrc to pDest, handling overlapping regions by detecting direction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if regions overlap (pSrc < pDest < pSrc+nLength)\n2. If forward copy is unsafe, copy backwards from end\n3. Optimize by copying dwords (4 bytes) when destination is aligned\n4. Handle misaligned start with byte copies until alignment\n5. Copy remaining bytes after main loop using switch statement fallthrough\n\nParameters:\n- pDest (void*): Destination buffer address\n- pSrc (void*): Source buffer address\n- nLength (uint): Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n- void*: pDest (destination pointer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3: Alignment mask (check for 4-byte alignment)\n- 0x2: Shift right 2 (convert byte count to dword count)\n- 7: Minimum dword count for loop optimization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
