      "name": "UnwindExceptionContext",
      "signature": "void UnwindExceptionContext(void * pExceptionRecord)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Unwinds exception context by calling local unwinder with two exception fields.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract two values from exception record at offsets 0x18 and 0x1c\n2. Push both values onto stack as arguments\n3. Call __local_unwind2 to perform stack unwinding\n4. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\n- pExceptionRecord (void*): Pointer to exception record structure containing unwind information at offsets 0x18 and 0x1c\n\nReturns:\n- void (performs unwinding as side effect)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18: Offset to first exception field in record\n- 0x1c: Offset to second exception field in record",
