      "name": "FileWriteData",
      "signature": "int FileWriteData(uint dwStreamId, char * lpszData, uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Writes data to a file stream with CRLF line ending conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return -1 if size is 0\n2. Get stream descriptor from global array using stream ID\n3. If stream is not in text mode, directly write buffer via WriteFile\n4. If text mode, scan buffer for LF characters and insert CR before each LF\n5. Write converted data in 1024-byte chunks\n6. Update error state via global callbacks on errors\n7. Return bytes successfully written (or error code)\n\nParameters:\n- dwStreamId (uint): Stream handle/ID\n- pbData (char*): Buffer containing data to write\n- nSize (uint): Number of bytes to write\n\nReturns:\n- Bytes written on success\n- -1 if size is 0\n- Error code on failure (from GetLastError)",
