      "name": "EnterCriticalSectionOrInitialize",
      "signature": "void EnterCriticalSectionOrInitialize(void * pSection)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Dispatches to critical section handler based on address range.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pSection pointer is within locked section range (0x6fab092f-0x6fab0b90)\n2. If in range: compute index via SAR and call InitializeLockedSection\n3. If not in range: call EnterCriticalSection directly\n4. Both paths initialize/enter the same critical section structure\n\nParameters:\n- pSection (void*): Pointer to critical section or locked section structure\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6fab092f: Lower bound of locked section range\n- 0x6fab0b90: Upper bound of locked section range\n- 0x9054f6d0: Offset adjustment for range calculation\n- 0x5 (5): Right shift amount for index computation\n- 0x1c (28): Base offset for locked section handler\n- 0x20 (32): Offset to critical section pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ff70d7fac2548b5958f726d1eeb33c1c",
