      "name": "LeaveCriticalSectionConditional",
      "signature": "void LeaveCriticalSectionConditional(int nSectionIndex, void * pObjectData)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Releases a critical section lock using conditional dispatch based on section index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nSectionIndex < 0x14 (20 decimal)\n2. If index is in global range (< 20): Add 0x1c (28) to index and call LeaveCriticalSectionByIndex\n3. If index is in object-embedded range (>= 20): Access CRITICAL_SECTION at pObjectData + 0x20 and call LeaveCriticalSection directly\n\nParameters:\n- nSectionIndex (int): Section index determining dispatch path\n  - 0-19: Uses global critical section array via indexed lookup (index + 28)\n  - >= 20: Uses object-embedded critical section at offset 0x20\n- pObjectData (void *): Pointer to object containing embedded CRITICAL_SECTION\n  - Only used when nSectionIndex >= 20\n  - CRITICAL_SECTION located at offset +0x20 from object base\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- pObjectData is only dereferenced when nSectionIndex >= 20\n- Index offset 0x1c (28) maps low indices to higher critical section array slots\n\nCalled From:\n- FUN_6faaaf63: Iterator that processes object array, releasing locks per object",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2221715ad392d22929a667a9021e3f90",
