      "name": "ConvertWideCharToMultiByteThreadSafe",
      "signature": "int ConvertWideCharToMultiByteThreadSafe(char * lpszBuffer, WCHAR wcChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Thread-safe wrapper for wide character to multibyte conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment global lock counter (g_nConversionLockCount) atomically\n2. Check if initialization flag (g_fConversionNeedsInit) is set\n3. If init needed: decrement lock counter and acquire critical section 0x13\n4. Call FUN_6faa9b34 to perform actual wide-to-multibyte conversion\n5. If critical section was acquired: release it via LeaveCriticalSectionByIndex\n6. Otherwise: decrement lock counter atomically\n7. Return conversion result (byte count or -1 on error)\n\nParameters:\n- lpszBuffer (char *): Output buffer for converted multibyte character\n- wcChar (WCHAR): Wide character to convert to multibyte\n\nReturns:\n- Number of bytes written to buffer (1-2 for MBCS, 1 for ASCII)\n- -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) on conversion error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Thread contention handled via InterlockedIncrement/Decrement\n- Critical section 0x13 used when initialization state is active\n- Inner function handles ASCII pass-through (chars < 0x100)\n\nCalled By:\n- FormatStringParser: During %c and %s wide-char format processing",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c85f8270e3f1487f07a5ecca3d9faf90",
