      "name": "AllocateZeroedMemory",
      "signature": "void * AllocateZeroedMemory(uint dwElementCount, uint dwElementSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates zeroed memory (calloc-style) with multiple allocation strategy fallback.\n\nClassification: Worker function - Core memory allocator called by exception handlers and TLS init\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total allocation size: dwTotalSize = dwElementCount * dwElementSize\n2. Validate size does not overflow (must be less than 0xFFFFFFE1)\n3. If requested size is 0, use minimum allocation of 1 byte\n4. Round size up to 16-byte alignment: (size + 0xF) AND 0xFFFFFFF0\n5. Enter allocation retry loop\n6. Try allocation based on g_nAllocationMode global:\n   Mode 3 (Block): Use AllocateMemoryBlock() if size <= g_dwMaxBufSize\n   Mode 2 (Pool): Use AllocateMemoryFromPool() if size <= g_dwCacheLimit\n7. On pool/block allocation failure, fall back to HeapAlloc with HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY\n8. If all allocations fail and g_pbOutOfMemory callback exists, call TryHandleOutOfMemory()\n9. Retry allocation if OOM handler returns success, else return NULL\n10. Zero allocated memory with memset() before returning\n\nParameters:\n- dwElementCount (uint): Number of elements to allocate\n- dwElementSize (uint): Size of each element in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void *: Pointer to zeroed memory block on success\n- NULL: On allocation failure after all strategies exhausted\n\nGlobals Used:\n- g_nAllocationMode: Allocation strategy (2=pool, 3=block)\n- g_dwMaxBufSize: Maximum size for block allocator\n- g_dwCacheLimit: Maximum size for pool allocator  \n- g_hProcessHeap: Process heap handle for HeapAlloc fallback\n- g_pbOutOfMemory: Out-of-memory handler presence flag\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero-size allocation returns 1-byte block (mimics CRT behavior)\n- Size overflow (>= 0xFFFFFFE1) skips all allocation attempts\n- Pool allocator uses 16-byte chunk index (size >> 4)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- AllocateMemoryBlock: Block allocator (mode 3)\n- AllocateMemoryFromPool: Pool allocator (mode 2)\n- TryHandleOutOfMemory: OOM recovery callback\n- InitializeLockedSection: Acquires critical section 9\n\nSEH Frame: Uses structured exception handling for thread safety during allocation",
