      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Releases the block allocator critical section (section index 9).\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Unlocks critical section 9 after block allocator operations\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push critical section index 9 onto stack\n2. Call LeaveCriticalSectionByIndex to release the lock\n3. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nCaller Context:\n- Called exclusively by AllocateZeroedMemory after AllocateMemoryBlock completes\n- Paired with InitializeLockedSection(9) which acquires the same critical section\n\nThread Safety:\n- This function is the unlock operation for the memory block allocator\n- Critical section 9 protects shared block allocator state during allocation",
