      "name": "StrCpyOptimized",
      "signature": "char * StrCpyOptimized(char * lpszDest, char * lpszSrc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Copy null-terminated string from source to destination.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Entry point for strcpy that jumps into StrCatOptimized's copy loop.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push EDI to save register (callee-save)\n2. Load destination pointer into EDI\n3. Jump to LAB_6faa9e41 in StrCatOptimized to execute optimized copy loop\n\nImplementation Notes:\n- This is an optimized CRT strcpy implementation\n- Reuses StrCatOptimized's DWORD-aligned copy loop at 0x6faa9e41\n- Skips strcat's \"find end of dest\" phase since strcpy writes from start\n- DWORD copy uses 0x7efefeff magic for null byte detection\n\nParameters:\n- lpszDest (char *): Destination buffer to receive copied string\n- lpszSrc (char *): Source null-terminated string to copy\n\nReturns:\n- char *: Pointer to lpszDest (original destination)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7efefeff: Null byte detection constant for DWORD scanning\n- 0x81010100: Mask for null byte presence check\n- 0x3: Alignment check mask (DWORD boundary)\n\nCallers:\n- OutputExceptionMessage: Copies program name and error strings\n- LoadEnvironmentVariablesArray: Copies environment variable strings",
