      "name": "StrCatOptimized",
      "signature": "char * StrCatOptimized(char * lpszDest, char * lpszSrc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Optimized string concatenation (strcat implementation).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Find end of destination string using DWORD-aligned scanning\n2. Handle unaligned prefix bytes by scanning byte-by-byte until aligned\n3. Use magic number technique (0x7efefeff XOR pattern) to detect null bytes in 4-byte chunks\n4. Once null found, calculate exact position within DWORD\n5. Copy source string to destination end using same alignment optimization\n6. Handle unaligned source prefix bytes by copying byte-by-byte\n7. Copy aligned DWORDs until null detected in source\n8. Write final partial DWORD with null terminator\n\nParameters:\nlpszDest - Pointer to destination string buffer (must have sufficient space)\nlpszSrc  - Pointer to null-terminated source string to append\n\nReturns:\nPointer to destination string (lpszDest)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7efefeff - Null byte detection constant (detects 0x00 in any byte position)\n0x81010100 - Mask for null byte detection result\n0xffffffff - XOR complement for null detection algorithm\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles unaligned pointers by byte-scanning until DWORD boundary\n- Detects null in any of 4 byte positions within DWORD\n- Copies 1-4 bytes for final partial DWORD based on null position\n\nSSA Variable Mapping:\npuVar3 (pchScanDest)   - Destination scan pointer during null search\npuVar5 (pchDestEnd)    - Pointer to destination string end\nuVar4  (dwScanValue)   - Current DWORD value being scanned\nuVar2  (dwSrcValue)    - Source DWORD for null detection\nbVar1  (chByte)        - Single byte during unaligned copy",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
