      "name": "InitializeCodePageCharacterClassTable",
      "signature": "void InitializeCodePageCharacterClassTable(int nCodePageType)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Initializes the character class table for a specified code page.\n\nBuilds a 257-byte character classification lookup table (g_abCharacterClassTable) used\nfor multibyte character string processing. Each byte in the table indicates character\nclass flags for that character code point.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock (index 0x19)\n2. Resolve code page type (-2=OEM, -3=ACP, -4=cached, else direct code page ID)\n3. If code page matches cached g_dwCurrentCodePage, return success immediately\n4. If code page is 0, fallback to default initialization\n5. Search g_adwKnownCodePageTable for known code page (932, 936, 949, 950, 1361)\n6. If found in known table:\n   a. Clear 257-byte character class table to zero\n   b. For each of 4 character categories, process byte range pairs\n   c. Set class bits (0x01, 0x02, 0x04, 0x08) for character ranges\n   d. Set g_fIsMultibyteCodePage = 1\n   e. Copy 12 bytes of flags from table entry\n   f. Lookup associated locale ID via FUN_6faaa0b7\n7. If not in known table, call GetCPInfo():\n   a. Clear character class table\n   b. If single-byte code page (MaxCharSize < 2), set g_fIsMultibyteCodePage = 0\n   c. If multibyte, process LeadByte ranges setting flag 0x04\n   d. Set flag 0x08 for all bytes 1-254 (valid trail bytes)\n   e. Clear flags 1-3 (no known code page specific data)\n8. Call FUN_6faaa113 to finalize\n9. Release critical section lock\n10. Return 0 on success, -1 on failure\n\nParameters:\n  nCodePageType - Code page type specifier:\n                  -2 = OEM code page (GetOEMCP)\n                  -3 = ANSI code page (GetACP)\n                  -4 = Use cached g_dwCodePage\n                  Other = Direct code page identifier (e.g., 932, 1252)\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) if GetCPInfo fails and g_fAllowFallbackCodePage is 0\n\nCharacter Class Flags (g_abCharClassMasks):\n  0x01 - Category 1 (ranges from table offset +0x10)\n  0x02 - Category 2 (ranges from table offset +0x18)\n  0x04 - Lead byte indicator (DBCS first byte)\n  0x08 - Valid trail byte (values 1-254 for DBCS)\n\nKnown Code Page Table Structure (48 bytes per entry):\n  Offset 0x00: DWORD dwCodePage\n  Offset 0x04: DWORD dwFlags1\n  Offset 0x08: DWORD dwFlags2\n  Offset 0x0C: DWORD dwFlags3\n  Offset 0x10: 8 bytes - Category 1 byte ranges (start,end pairs)\n  Offset 0x18: 8 bytes - Category 2 byte ranges\n  Offset 0x20: 8 bytes - Category 3 byte ranges\n  Offset 0x28: 8 bytes - Category 4 byte ranges\n\nSupported Known Code Pages:\n  932 (0x3A4) - Japanese Shift-JIS -> Locale 0x411\n  936 (0x3A8) - Simplified Chinese GBK -> Locale 0x804\n  949 (0x3B5) - Korean -> Locale 0x412\n  950 (0x3B6) - Traditional Chinese Big5 -> Locale 0x404\n  1361 (0x551) - Korean Johab",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b7003782678f33a2ea4e8b0cc2bae15e",
