      "name": "ResolveSpecialCodePage",
      "signature": "uint ResolveSpecialCodePage(int nCodePageId)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Resolves special code page identifiers to actual Windows code page values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear g_fCodePageFromSpecial flag to 0\n2. If nCodePageId == -2 (CP_OEMCP): Set flag to 1, return GetOEMCP()\n3. If nCodePageId == -3 (CP_ACP): Set flag to 1, return GetACP()\n4. If nCodePageId == -4 (thread locale): Set flag to 1, return g_dwCodePage\n5. Otherwise: Return nCodePageId unchanged (flag remains 0)\n\nParameters:\n  nCodePageId - Code page identifier. Special values:\n    -2 (0xFFFFFFFE): Use OEM code page (GetOEMCP)\n    -3 (0xFFFFFFFD): Use ANSI code page (GetACP)\n    -4 (0xFFFFFFFC): Use cached thread locale code page\n    Other: Return as-is (literal code page number)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Resolved Windows code page identifier (e.g., 437, 1252, 65001)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Sets g_fCodePageFromSpecial to 1 if a special code page was resolved\n  - Sets g_fCodePageFromSpecial to 0 if literal code page was passed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  -2 (CP_OEMCP): OEM code page constant\n  -3 (CP_ACP): ANSI code page constant  \n  -4: Thread/locale code page (custom constant)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
