      "name": "MapCodePageToLanguageId",
      "signature": "uint MapCodePageToLanguageId(uint dwCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Maps Windows code page identifiers to corresponding language identifiers (LangID).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if code page is 932 (Japanese Shift-JIS), return 0x411 (Japanese)\n2. Check if code page is 936 (Chinese Simplified GBK), return 0x804 (Chinese Simplified)\n3. Check if code page is 949 (Korean), return 0x412 (Korean)\n4. Check if code page is 950 (Chinese Traditional Big5), return 0x404 (Chinese Traditional)\n5. For unrecognized code pages, return 0 (no language mapping)\n\nParameters:\n  dwCodePage - Windows code page identifier (e.g., 932, 936, 949, 950)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Language ID (LangID) for recognized CJK code pages:\n         0x411 = Japanese (LANG_JAPANESE)\n         0x804 = Chinese Simplified (LANG_CHINESE_SIMPLIFIED)\n         0x412 = Korean (LANG_KOREAN)\n         0x404 = Chinese Traditional (LANG_CHINESE_TRADITIONAL)\n         0x0   = Unrecognized code page\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  Code Pages:\n    0x3a4 (932)  - Japanese Shift-JIS\n    0x3a8 (936)  - Chinese Simplified GBK\n    0x3b5 (949)  - Korean\n    0x3b6 (950)  - Chinese Traditional Big5\n  Language IDs:\n    0x411 (1041) - LANG_JAPANESE\n    0x804 (2052) - LANG_CHINESE_SIMPLIFIED\n    0x412 (1042) - LANG_KOREAN\n    0x404 (1028) - LANG_CHINESE_TRADITIONAL\n\nNote: Uses cascading subtraction for efficient switch implementation.",
