      "name": "ClearCodePageCharacterClassTable",
      "signature": "void ClearCodePageCharacterClassTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Clears the code page character class table and resets all code page state globals.\n\nCalled when code page initialization fails or when resetting to default state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear g_abCharacterClassTable (257 bytes: 0x40 DWORDs + 1 byte) using REP STOSD/STOSB\n2. Clear g_dwCurrentCodePage to indicate no code page active\n3. Clear g_fCodePageInitialized flag to indicate table invalid\n4. Clear g_dwCodePageLanguageId (language identifier)\n5. Clear g_dwCodePageProperty1, Property2, Property3 (code page flags from table)\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called when dwCodePage is 0 in InitializeCodePageCharacterClassTable\n- Called when GetCPInfo fails but g_fCodePageFromSpecial is set\n\nMemory Layout Cleared:\n  0x6fabdce0: g_abCharacterClassTable[257] - Character class lookup table\n  0x6fabdbc8: g_dwCurrentCodePage - Active code page number\n  0x6fabdbdc: g_fCodePageInitialized - Table validity flag\n  0x6fabdde4: g_dwCodePageLanguageId - Associated language ID\n  0x6fabdbd0-0x6fabdbd8: Code page property flags (3 DWORDs)\n\nDecompiler Variables (register-only, no stack storage):\n  iVar1 (nClearCount): ECX loop counter, counts down from 0x40\n  puVar2 (pTableEntry): EDI pointer, walks through table during clear\n\nAssembly Notes:\n- Uses STOSD.REP to clear 0x40 DWORDs (256 bytes) efficiently\n- Uses STOSB to clear final byte (total 257 bytes for 0-255 + sentinel)\n- Three consecutive STOSD instructions clear property flags at 0x6fabdbd0",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:05d3556ba26e52c51954a1255d97c525",
