      "name": "EnsureEnvironmentInitialized",
      "signature": "void EnsureEnvironmentInitialized(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Ensures environment initialization is performed exactly once.\n\nThis is an initialization guard function that checks if the environment\nhas already been initialized and, if not, triggers initialization of\nthe code page character class table with ANSI code page (-3).\n\nClassification: Initialization Guard (one-shot)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_fEnvInitialized flag\n2. If flag is 0 (not initialized):\n   a. Call InitializeCodePageCharacterClassTable(-3) to initialize with ANSI code page\n   b. Set g_fEnvInitialized = 1 to prevent future re-initialization\n3. Return immediately if already initialized\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nCallers:\n  LoadEnvironmentVariablesArray - called before processing environment strings\n  InitializeResourceBuffer - called before loading module resources\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  -3: ANSI code page specifier (GetACP) passed to InitializeCodePageCharacterClassTable\n  0x6fabef50: Address of g_fEnvInitialized flag\n\nThread Safety:\n  Not thread-safe. Multiple threads could race on first initialization.\n  Callers should ensure single-threaded initialization context.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:750c71b47c1aaa7e04385ca0c70f7831",
