      "name": "__alloca_probe",
      "signature": "void __alloca_probe(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "MSVC stack allocation probe - safely allocates stack space by touching pages incrementally.\n\nClassification: Runtime Utility (compiler-generated stack probe)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Receive allocation size in EAX (IMPLICIT parameter)\n2. Calculate stack pointer offset from current ESP\n3. If allocation size > 4096 (0x1000):\n   a. Loop: subtract page size from target pointer\n   b. Loop: subtract page size from remaining size\n   c. Loop: touch page via TEST [ECX],EAX to ensure page is committed\n   d. Loop: continue while remaining size >= 4096\n4. Subtract remaining size from target pointer\n5. Touch final page to ensure commitment\n6. Move ESP to new stack position\n7. Restore ECX from old stack frame\n8. Load return address from old stack location\n9. Push return address and return (transfers control back to caller)\n\nParameters:\n  EAX (IMPLICIT): dwAllocationSize - Number of bytes to allocate on stack\n\nReturns:\n  ESP modified to allocate requested stack space\n  EAX preserved (contains return address temporarily)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Small allocations (<= 4096 bytes): Single page touch, no loop\n- Large allocations (> 4096 bytes): Iterative page-by-page touch to avoid stack overflow\n- Each page touch via TEST instruction triggers page fault if uncommitted, causing OS to commit page\n\nCalled By:\n- GetMsvcrtHeapSelection: Large local buffer allocation\n- GetStringTypeExWrapper: Stack buffer for string operations  \n- LCMapStringExWrapper: Stack buffer for locale mapping\n\nTechnical Notes:\n- This is a compiler intrinsic generated by MSVC for large stack allocations\n- The probe prevents stack overflow by ensuring each page between current ESP and target is committed\n- Windows uses guard pages; touching pages in order allows OS to extend stack properly\n- Without probing, jumping over guard page causes immediate stack overflow exception",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2a518bd4b0b93e6cf2e2d91eb6ff7bf6",
