      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Display MessageBox using dynamically loaded user32.dll functions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if MessageBoxA function pointer is already cached in g_pfnMessageBoxA\n2. If not cached, load user32.dll via LoadLibraryA\n3. Resolve MessageBoxA address via GetProcAddress and cache in g_pfnMessageBoxA\n4. Resolve GetActiveWindow and GetLastActivePopup, cache in globals\n5. If MessageBoxA resolution fails, return 0\n6. Call GetActiveWindow to get current active window handle (hwndParent)\n7. If hwndParent valid, call GetLastActivePopup to get topmost popup window\n8. Call MessageBoxA with resolved parent window handle and parameters\n9. Return MessageBoxA result (button clicked by user)\n\nParameters:\n- lpszText (char *): Message text to display in the dialog body\n- lpszCaption (char *): Caption/title for the message box window\n- dwType (uint): Message box style flags (MB_OK=0, MB_ICONERROR=0x10, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n- int: MessageBoxA return value indicating button clicked (IDOK=1, IDCANCEL=2, etc.)\n- 0: If user32.dll load failed or MessageBoxA could not be resolved\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First call incurs LoadLibrary overhead; subsequent calls use cached pointers\n- Parent window is NULL (0) if GetActiveWindow returns NULL or is not cached\n- GetLastActivePopup only called if GetActiveWindow returns valid handle\n\nGlobals Used:\n- g_pfnMessageBoxA (FARPROC): Cached MessageBoxA function pointer at 0x6fabda28\n- g_pfnGetActiveWindow (FARPROC): Cached GetActiveWindow function pointer at 0x6fabda2c\n- g_pfnGetLastActivePopup (FARPROC): Cached GetLastActivePopup function pointer at 0x6fabda30\n\nDecompiler Variables:\n- iVar1 (nResult): Holds window handle, then final MessageBoxA return value\n- hModule: user32.dll module handle from LoadLibraryA",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
