      "name": "IsReadableMemory",
      "signature": "bool IsReadableMemory(void * pMemory, dword cbSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Validates that a memory region is readable.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize ESI with 1 (true) as default return value\n2. Push size (cbSize) and address (pMemory) parameters for IsBadReadPtr\n3. Call IsBadReadPtr to check if memory is accessible\n4. Test result (EAX): if zero, memory is readable; if non-zero, memory is bad\n5. If IsBadReadPtr returned non-zero (bad), set ESI to 0 (false)\n6. Return ESI (true = readable, false = not readable)\n\nParameters:\n- pMemory (void*): Pointer to the memory region to validate\n- cbSize (dword): Size in bytes of the memory region to check\n\nReturns:\n- bool: true (1) if memory is readable, false (0) if memory is invalid\n\nNotes:\n- Wrapper around Windows API IsBadReadPtr with inverted return semantics\n- IsBadReadPtr returns 0 on success (memory good), non-zero on failure\n- This function inverts that logic: returns true when IsBadReadPtr returns 0\n- Used by SEH exception handlers to validate exception records before access\n- Called from ProcessSEHException and DispatchSehHandler for pointer validation\n- Classification: Leaf utility function - validates memory before dereferencing",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
