      "name": "IsMemoryWritable",
      "signature": "bool IsMemoryWritable(void * pMemory, dword cbSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Validates that a memory region is writable.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call IsBadWritePtr to test if memory range is writable\n2. Invert result: IsBadWritePtr returns non-zero if BAD, we return true if GOOD\n\nParameters:\n- pMemory (void *): Pointer to start of memory region to validate\n- cbSize (dword): Size in bytes of the memory region to check\n\nReturns:\n- true (1): Memory region is writable and safe to access\n- false (0): Memory region is not writable or invalid\n\nCalled By:\n- DispatchSehHandler: Validates SEH exception record and context pointers before access\n\nNotes:\n- Wrapper function that inverts IsBadWritePtr semantics for positive logic\n- IsBadWritePtr returns 0 if memory IS writable, non-zero if NOT writable\n- This function returns true if writable, false if not writable",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
