      "name": "IsValidCodePointer",
      "signature": "bool IsValidCodePointer(FARPROC pfnCodePointer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Validates whether a function pointer references executable code.\n\nWrapper around Windows API IsBadCodePtr with inverted return semantics.\nIsBadCodePtr returns TRUE if pointer is invalid; this function inverts\nthat to return TRUE when pointer IS valid (safe to call).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call IsBadCodePtr with the provided function pointer\n2. Return TRUE if IsBadCodePtr returned FALSE (pointer is valid)\n3. Return FALSE if IsBadCodePtr returned TRUE (pointer is invalid)\n\nParameters:\n  pfnCodePointer - FARPROC function pointer to validate\n\nReturns:\n  bool - TRUE if pointer is valid and callable, FALSE otherwise\n\nCallers:\n  DispatchSehHandler - validates exception handler before dispatch\n  FilterCppException - validates filter function pointer\n\nNote: IsBadCodePtr probes memory at the pointer location. While it can\ndetect obviously invalid pointers, it cannot guarantee the target is\nactually valid executable code - only that reading from it won't fault.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:327465fd6eeb9f68fc596f7e865a96c5",
