      "name": "SMemMove",
      "signature": "void * SMemMove(void * pDest, void * pSrc, uint dwByteCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Memory move with overlapping region support (memmove implementation).\n\nCopies nByteCount bytes from pSrc to pDest, correctly handling overlapping\nmemory regions by choosing forward or backward copy direction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check for overlap: if (pSrc < pDest && pDest < pSrc + nByteCount)\n2. If overlap detected (dest within source range):\n   a. Copy backward from high addresses to low addresses\n   b. Start at end of both buffers (pSrc + nByteCount - 4, pDest + nByteCount - 4)\n   c. Align destination to DWORD boundary by copying 1-3 trailing bytes first\n   d. Use REP MOVSD for bulk DWORD copies (STD direction flag set)\n   e. Handle remaining 0-3 bytes at start of buffer\n3. If no overlap (forward copy safe):\n   a. Copy forward from low addresses to high addresses\n   b. Align destination to DWORD boundary by copying 1-3 leading bytes first\n   c. Use REP MOVSD for bulk DWORD copies (CLD direction flag)\n   d. Handle remaining 0-3 bytes at end of buffer\n4. Small copies (< 8 DWORDs) use unrolled switch-based copy for efficiency\n\nParameters:\n  pDest      - void *  - Destination buffer pointer\n  pSrc       - void *  - Source buffer pointer  \n  nByteCount - uint    - Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n  void * - Returns pDest (original destination pointer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero-length copy returns pDest immediately\n  - Non-overlapping regions always use forward copy (faster)\n  - Small copies (1-7 DWORDs) use Duff's device style unrolled loop\n  - Handles all alignment cases (dest aligned, dest misaligned by 1/2/3 bytes)\n\nCallers:\n  - DispatchSehHandler - Exception handling memory operations\n  - FreeAllocatedBlock - Memory block management",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:bff09423b51fd121ea30afec957819f4",
