      "name": "FatalExceptionExit",
      "signature": "void FatalExceptionExit(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Fatal exception exit handler - terminates process after exception handling fails.\n\nCalled when the registered exception handler (if any) has executed and the\nexception remains unhandled. This is the final cleanup path that outputs\nan error message and terminates the process.\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Fatal Error Handler (does not return)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Output runtime error message for exception type 0x0A (abnormal termination)\n2. Dispatch signal handler for SIGABRT (signal 22/0x16)\n3. Terminate process with exit code 3\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- Does not return - calls __exit(3)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ExecuteExceptionHandler: Sole caller, invokes after exception handler runs\n- OutputExceptionMessage: Displays runtime error dialog/stderr message\n- FUN_6faab558: Signal handler dispatcher (SIGABRT = 0x16)\n- __exit: C runtime process termination\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0A (10): Exception type for abnormal program termination\n- 0x16 (22): SIGABRT signal number\n- 0x03: Exit code indicating abnormal termination",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
