      "name": "GetOsErrorPointer",
      "signature": "uint * GetOsErrorPointer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Returns pointer to thread-local OS error code storage.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetExceptionHandlerContext to get thread-local handler context\n2. Return pointer at offset 0x0c (12 bytes) from context base\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses thread-local storage internally)\n\nReturns:\n- uint* - Pointer to OS error code storage location in handler context\n\nHandler Context Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type    Description\n  0x00    4     dwThreadId         uint    Thread ID\n  0x04    4     dwSentinel         uint    Sentinel (0xffffffff)\n  0x08    4     dwUnknown          uint    Reserved/unknown\n  0x0c    4     dwOsError          uint    OS error code (this function returns pointer here)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GetExceptionHandlerContext: Returns base of handler context\n- GetErrnoPointer: Returns errno storage (different from OS error)\n- MapOsErrorToErrno: Stores OS error here then maps to errno",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
