      "name": "CloseStreamDescriptor",
      "signature": "int CloseStreamDescriptor(uint dwStreamIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Closes a stream descriptor entry and invalidates its file handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwStreamIndex is less than g_nStreamCount\n2. Calculate bucket index (dwStreamIndex >> 5) and entry offset ((dwStreamIndex & 0x1f) * 0x24)\n3. Get pointer to stream descriptor from g_apStreamDescriptors[bucket] + offset\n4. Check stream is open: descriptor flags bit 0 must be set AND handle != -1\n5. If fCrashHandlerActive == 1, clear standard handle for stdin/stdout/stderr:\n   - Index 0: STD_INPUT_HANDLE (0xFFFFFFF6 = -10)\n   - Index 1: STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE (0xFFFFFFF5 = -11)\n   - Index 2: STD_ERROR_HANDLE (0xFFFFFFF4 = -12)\n6. Invalidate descriptor by setting handle field to -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n7. Return 0 on success\n\nParameters:\n- dwStreamIndex (uint): Index into stream descriptor table (0=stdin, 1=stdout, 2=stderr, 3+ user streams)\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success - stream descriptor closed\n- -1: Error - invalid index or stream not open (sets errno to EBADF=9)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Clears Windows standard handles only when crash handler is active\n- Stream indices 0/1/2 correspond to standard I/O handles\n- Error sets errno=9 (EBADF - Bad file descriptor) and clears OS error\n\nStream Descriptor Layout (0x24 bytes per entry):\nOffset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n0x00    4     hFile       int     File handle (-1 = invalid)\n0x04    1     bFlags      byte    Stream flags (bit 0 = open)\n\nSSA Variables:\n- piVar1 (pnDescriptor): Pointer to stream descriptor handle field\n- iVar3 (nEntryOffset): Calculated offset within bucket (index * 0x24)\n- pDVar2 (pdwErrnoPtr): Pointer to errno/OS error field\n- nStdHandle (dwStdHandle): Windows standard handle constant\n\nGlobal References:\n- g_nStreamCount: Maximum valid stream index\n- g_apStreamDescriptors: Array of bucket pointers to descriptor arrays\n- fCrashHandlerActive: Flag indicating crash handler state",
