      "name": "GetStreamFileHandle",
      "signature": "dword GetStreamFileHandle(dword nStreamIdx)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Retrieves the OS file handle from a stream descriptor given a stream index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if stream index is within valid range (< g_nStreamCount)\n2. Compute bucket index (nStreamIdx >> 5) and offset within bucket (nStreamIdx & 0x1F)\n3. Calculate descriptor offset: offset * 0x24 (36-byte stride per descriptor)\n4. Check stream validity flag at descriptor+4, bit 0 (0x01)\n5. If stream is valid, return file handle from descriptor base (offset 0)\n6. If invalid stream: set errno to 9 (EBADF), clear OS error, return 0xFFFFFFFF\n\nParameters:\n- nStreamIdx (dword): Stream index into the stream descriptor table\n\nReturns:\n- File handle (HANDLE cast to dword) on success\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) on error (invalid stream index or closed stream)\n\nStructure Layout (Stream Descriptor, 36 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n0x00    4     hFile           HANDLE  OS file handle\n0x04    1     bFlags          byte    Stream state flags (bit 0 = valid/open)\n...     31    (other fields)  -       Buffer, position, mode flags\n\nError Handling:\n- Sets errno to 9 (EBADF - bad file descriptor) via GetErrnoPointer()\n- Clears OS error via FUN_6faaad04() (GetDosErrorPointer + offset 3)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1F: Mask for offset within 32-entry bucket\n- 5: Right shift for bucket index (32 entries per bucket)\n- 0x24: Stream descriptor stride (36 bytes)\n- 0x04: Offset to flags byte in descriptor\n- 0x01: Bit mask for \"stream valid/open\" flag\n- 9: EBADF errno value (bad file descriptor)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
