      "comment": "Flushes a stream buffer to disk, optionally committing to OS file buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call internal buffer flush (FUN_6faaaefe) to write pending data\n2. If internal flush fails, return -1 (error)\n3. Check commit flag (0x40) at stream offset +0xd\n4. If commit flag set, call OS-level FlushFileBuffers via FUN_6faab794\n5. Return 0 on success, -1 on any failure\n\nParameters:\n  pStreamBuffer - Pointer to stream buffer structure\n    +0x00: Current buffer position (int)\n    +0x04: Buffer count/index (int)\n    +0x08: Base buffer pointer (int)\n    +0x0C: Flags word (includes mode bits)\n    +0x0D: Extended flags byte (0x40 = commit to disk)\n    +0x10: File handle/stream descriptor (param_1[4])\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Success (buffer flushed, optionally committed)\n  -1 - Error (internal flush failed or OS sync failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If commit flag (0x40) not set, only internal buffer is flushed\n  - NEG/SBB pattern converts FlushFileBuffers result to 0/-1\n\nClassification: Worker function - called by stream iteration to flush buffers",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:0db91ea76f5c7c9fd0bef446c106db61",
