      "name": "CommitStreamBufferWrite",
      "signature": "int CommitStreamBufferWrite(int * pStreamContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Commits pending buffered data to underlying stream and resets buffer state.\n\nClassification: Worker function - called by FlushStreamBuffer and stream close operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check stream mode bits (flags & 0x3) == 2 (write mode)\n2. Check if stream has active write buffer (flags & 0x108)\n3. Calculate pending bytes: current_position - buffer_base\n4. If pending bytes > 0, call WriteStreamData with stream ID, buffer base, and size\n5. If write succeeded (bytes written == pending): Clear dirty bit if set (flags &= ~0x02)\n6. If write failed: Set error flag (flags |= 0x20), return -1\n7. Reset buffer count to 0 (pStreamContext[1] = 0)\n8. Reset current position to buffer base (pStreamContext[0] = pStreamContext[2])\n\nParameters:\n- pStreamContext (int*): Pointer to stream context structure\n  - [0] (offset 0x00): Current write position\n  - [1] (offset 0x04): Buffer count/offset\n  - [2] (offset 0x08): Buffer base address\n  - [3] (offset 0x0C): Mode and status flags\n  - [4] (offset 0x10): Stream ID for WriteStreamData\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success or no data to flush\n- -1 on write error\n\nFlag Bits (offset 0x0C):\n- 0x03 mask: Stream mode (2 = write mode)\n- 0x02: Dirty flag (buffer modified)\n- 0x20: Error flag\n- 0x80: Binary mode flag\n- 0x100: Buffered output flag\n- 0x108: Combined buffered output check\n\nCallers: FlushStreamBuffer, FUN_6faab748 (stream close)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
