      "name": "FlushAllStreamBuffers",
      "signature": "int FlushAllStreamBuffers(int nFlushMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes all open stream buffers based on flush mode parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize counters (nFlushedCount=0, nErrorFlag=0)\n2. Acquire global stream array lock (critical section index 2)\n3. Loop through all stream slots (0 to g_nStreamCount-1):\n   a. Get stream buffer pointer from g_pStreamBufferArray[nStreamIndex]\n   b. Skip if NULL or stream flags (offset 0x0C) don't have 0x83 bits set\n   c. Acquire per-stream lock via FUN_6faa99e8\n   d. Re-check stream flags after lock acquisition\n   e. If nFlushMode == 1 (count mode):\n      - Flush stream buffer\n      - On success, increment nFlushedCount\n   f. If nFlushMode == 0 (error mode) AND write flag (0x02) set:\n      - Flush stream buffer\n      - On failure, set nErrorFlag = -1\n   g. Release per-stream lock via LeaveCriticalSectionConditional\n4. Release global stream array lock\n5. Return nFlushedCount if mode 1, else return nErrorFlag\n\nParameters:\n- nFlushMode (int): Flush operation mode\n  - 0: Flush dirty streams (write flag 0x02 set), return -1 on any error\n  - 1: Flush all active streams, return count of successful flushes\n\nReturns:\n- int: Mode 1: Number of successfully flushed streams (>= 0)\n       Mode 0: 0 on success, -1 if any flush failed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x83: Stream active flags mask (bit 0x01=open, 0x02=write, 0x80=modified)\n- 0x02: Write mode flag at stream buffer offset 0x0C\n- 2: Global stream array critical section index\n- 0x0C: Offset to stream flags field in stream buffer structure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_nStreamCount <= 0, loop is skipped entirely\n- Stream flags are checked twice (before and after lock acquisition) to handle races\n- Only streams with 0x83 flags set are processed",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e7b052927c73f8415c227814d8219b82",
