      "signature": "int StringNLength(char * lpszString, int nMaxCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "StringNLength - Calculate length of null-terminated string with maximum bound\n\nFUNCTION CLASSIFICATION: Leaf function / Internal utility\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize current pointer to start of string and remaining count to max\n  2. If max count is 0, skip loop entirely\n  3. Loop: Decrement remaining count, check if current byte is null terminator\n  4. If null found, break out of loop early\n  5. Otherwise advance pointer and continue if count not exhausted\n  6. After loop: If current byte is null, return pointer difference (actual length)\n  7. If no null found within limit, return original max count\n\nParameters:\n  lpszString (char *) - Pointer to null-terminated string to measure\n  nMaxCount (int) - Maximum number of characters to scan\n\nReturns:\n  int - Length of string if null terminator found within nMaxCount bytes\n      - nMaxCount if no null terminator found within limit\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - nMaxCount == 0: Returns 0 immediately (no scanning)\n  - Empty string (*lpszString == 0): Returns 0\n  - String longer than nMaxCount: Returns nMaxCount (truncated)\n\nCaller Context:\n  Called by LCMapStringExWrapper to calculate actual string length\n  before locale mapping operations when cchSrc > 0\n\nEquivalent To: strnlen(lpszString, nMaxCount)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c365f0335b7bc4452623cbc78de16e67",
