      "name": "ToUpperWithLocale",
      "signature": "uint ToUpperWithLocale(uint dwCharCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts a character to uppercase with locale awareness and thread-safety.\n\nClassification: Public API / Worker function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if locale conversion is needed (g_fConversionNeedsInit == 0)\n2. Fast path (no locale): Check if char is lowercase ASCII (0x61-0x7a)\n   - If lowercase ASCII: subtract 0x20 to convert to uppercase\n   - Otherwise: return unchanged\n3. Slow path (locale-aware):\n   a. Increment lock count (InterlockedIncrement on g_nConversionLockCount)\n   b. Double-check if initialization still needed (g_fConversionNeedsInit at 0x6fabdbc0)\n   c. If init needed: decrement lock, call InitializeLockedSection(0x13)\n   d. Call ToUpperWithLocaleInternal for actual conversion\n   e. Clean up: LeaveCriticalSectionByIndex(0x13) or InterlockedDecrement\n\nParameters:\n  dwCharCode (uint) - Character code to convert to uppercase\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Uppercase version of character, or unchanged if not lowercase\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - ASCII 'a'-'z' (0x61-0x7a): Fast path converts to 'A'-'Z' (0x41-0x5a)\n  - Non-lowercase or locale-dependent: Uses LCMapStringEx via ToUpperWithLocaleInternal\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x61 - ASCII 'a'\n  0x7a - ASCII 'z'\n  0x20 - Difference between lowercase and uppercase ASCII\n  0x13 - Critical section index for locale conversion\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_fConversionNeedsInit (0x6fabda4c) - Flag: 0 = fast ASCII path, non-zero = use locale\n  g_fConversionNeedsInit (0x6fabdbc0) - Secondary init flag checked under lock\n  g_nConversionLockCount (0x6fabdbc4) - Interlocked reference count for conversion lock\n\nCallers:\n  StringToLongInternal - Uses for hex digit conversion (A-F to a-f equivalence)",
