      "name": "ToUpperWithLocaleInternal",
      "signature": "uint ToUpperWithLocaleInternal(void * this, uint dwCharCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Internal helper for locale-aware uppercase conversion.\n\nCalled by ToUpperWithLocale after acquiring the conversion critical section lock.\nConverts a single character to uppercase using either fast ASCII path or\nlocale-specific LCMapStringExWrapper for multi-byte character sets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If locale conversion not initialized (g_fConversionNeedsInit == 0):\n   a. Fast ASCII path: if character in range 'a'-'z' (0x61-0x7a), subtract 0x20\n   b. Otherwise return character unchanged\n2. If locale conversion active:\n   a. For single-byte chars (< 0x100), check if lowercase via character class table\n      - If g_nMaxCharSize < 2, use direct table lookup (bit 0x02 = lowercase)\n      - Else call FUN_6faab4e3 for multi-byte aware check\n   b. If not lowercase, return unchanged\n   c. Prepare character for LCMapString:\n      - Check high byte in char class table for lead byte marker (0x80)\n      - If single byte: store in param_1[0], length = 1\n      - If double byte (DBCS): swap bytes for proper order, length = 2\n   d. Call LCMapStringExWrapper with LCMAP_UPPERCASE (0x200)\n   e. Extract result based on returned length (1 or 2 bytes)\n\nParameters:\n  this (void *) - IMPLICIT: Unused ECX parameter from thiscall convention\n  dwCharCode (uint) - Character code to convert (single or multi-byte packed)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Uppercase character code, or original if no conversion needed/possible\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - ASCII lowercase (0x61-0x7a): Direct subtraction, no API call\n  - Non-lowercase characters: Return unchanged\n  - DBCS lead bytes: Detected via 0x80 flag in char class table\n  - LCMapStringExWrapper failure: Returns original character\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x61 ('a'), 0x7a ('z') - ASCII lowercase range\n  0x20 - Offset between lowercase/uppercase ASCII\n  0x100 - Single-byte character threshold\n  0x02 - Lowercase bit flag in character class table\n  0x80 - DBCS lead byte flag in character class table\n  0x200 - LCMAP_UPPERCASE flag for LCMapString\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_fConversionNeedsInit (0x6fabda4c) - Locale ID when conversion active, 0 if not\n  g_nMaxCharSize (0x6fab11e4) - Max bytes per character for current code page\n  g_abCharClassTable (0x6fab0bc8) - Character classification lookup table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
