      "name": "FlushStreamWithLock",
      "signature": "int FlushStreamWithLock(int * pStreamState)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes stream with critical section protection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize return value to -1 (error/uninitialized)\n2. Check if stream disabled flag (0x40) is set at offset +0x0C\n3. If disabled: Clear flags at offset +0x0C and return -1\n4. If enabled: Enter critical section, call FlushStreamInternal, leave critical section\n5. Return result from FlushStreamInternal\n\nParameters:\n- pStreamState (int *): Pointer to stream state structure\n  - Offset +0x0C: Flags byte, bit 6 (0x40) = stream disabled\n  - Offset +0x20: CRITICAL_SECTION for thread safety\n\nReturns:\n- int: Result from FlushStreamInternal, or -1 if stream disabled\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If stream disabled (flag 0x40 set), clears all flags and returns -1 without flushing\n\nFlag Bits (offset +0x0C):\n- 0x40: Stream disabled - skip flush, clear flags only\n- 0x83: Used by FlushStreamInternal for flush decision",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e9b7e334c31a0ed876fb0ca3fc54ed48",
