      "name": "FlushStreamInternal",
      "signature": "int FlushStreamInternal(int * pStreamState)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes stream buffer and synchronizes with file descriptor.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize result to -1 (error/uninitialized)\n2. Check stream flags at offset +0x0C for flush requirement (0x83 mask)\n3. If flags indicate active stream (read/write mode or dirty):\n   a. Commit pending buffer writes via CommitStreamBufferWrite\n   b. Free dynamic buffer if allocated via FreeStreamBufferIfDynamic\n   c. Synchronize underlying file descriptor via SyncStreamDescriptor\n   d. If sync fails (returns < 0), reset result to -1\n   e. If sync succeeds and temp buffer at offset +0x1C exists:\n      - Free temp buffer via ProcessAllocatedMemory\n      - Clear temp buffer pointer\n4. Clear all flags at offset +0x0C\n5. Return result (0 success, -1 error)\n\nParameters:\n- pStreamState (int *): Pointer to stream state structure\n  - Offset +0x0C (byte): Stream flags\n  - Offset +0x10: File descriptor index\n  - Offset +0x1C: Temporary buffer pointer\n\nReturns:\n- int: 0 on success, -1 on error or if stream not active\n\nFlag Bits (offset +0x0C, 0x83 mask):\n- 0x01: Read mode active\n- 0x02: Write mode active  \n- 0x80: Buffer dirty/needs flush\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If flags & 0x83 == 0, skips flush and just clears flags\n- Temp buffer at +0x1C freed only on successful sync",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:eb7ebe8853ab4246d611f1ee5af2c48e",
