      "name": "SyncStreamFileBuffers",
      "signature": "int SyncStreamFileBuffers(uint dwStreamIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Synchronizes stream file buffers to disk via Windows FlushFileBuffers API.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwStreamIndex against g_nStreamCount; if invalid, set errno=EBADF and return -1\n2. Calculate bucket index (dwStreamIndex >> 5) and slot offset ((dwStreamIndex & 0x1F) * 0x24)\n3. Check stream active flag (bit 0 at descriptor offset +4); if inactive, goto error\n4. Acquire stream lock via AcquireStreamLock\n5. Re-check active flag under lock (double-check locking pattern)\n6. Get file handle via GetStreamFileHandle\n7. Call FlushFileBuffers to sync OS buffers to disk\n8. On FlushFileBuffers failure, get OS error via GetLastError and store in GetOsErrorPointer\n9. On any failure path, set errno=9 (EBADF) and return -1\n10. Release stream lock via ReleaseStreamLock\n11. Return 0 on success, -1 on failure\n\nParameters:\n  dwStreamIndex - Stream descriptor index (0 to g_nStreamCount-1)\n                  Index is decomposed: bucket = index >> 5, slot = (index & 0x1F) * 0x24\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Success (file buffers synchronized to disk)\n  -1 - Error (invalid index, inactive stream, or FlushFileBuffers failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Double-check locking: active flag checked before and after acquiring lock\n  - Stream descriptor stride is 0x24 (36 bytes), organized in buckets of 32\n  - errno set to 9 (EBADF) for all error conditions\n\nError Handling:\n  - Invalid stream index: set errno=EBADF, return -1 immediately\n  - Inactive stream (before lock): set errno=EBADF, return -1\n  - Inactive stream (after lock): set errno=EBADF, return -1\n  - FlushFileBuffers failure: store OS error, set errno=EBADF, return -1\n\nStream Descriptor Structure (partial):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Description\n  +0x04   1     flags        Bit 0 = stream active flag\n\nSSA Variable Mapping (decompiler temporaries, cannot be renamed):\n  hFile            - HANDLE from GetStreamFileHandle\n  BVar1            - BOOL result from FlushFileBuffers  \n  DVar1/DVar2      - OS error code from GetLastError\n  iVar4/iVar5      - Calculated slot offset within bucket\n  pDVar3/pDVar4    - Pointer to errno storage\n  puVar2/puVar3    - Pointer to OS error storage\n\nClassification: Worker function - called by FlushStreamBuffer when commit flag set",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b14dfb771e9c85951130aa7c0ee6e7bc",
