      "name": "UTIL_StringCountSpanComplement",
      "signature": "int UTIL_StringCountSpanComplement(char * lpszString, char * lpszCharSet)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Counts characters in string before any character from charset appears (strcspn implementation).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 32-byte (256-bit) character set bitmap to all zeros on stack\n2. For each character in lpszCharSet:\n   a. Read character byte value\n   b. If null terminator, exit bitmap building loop\n   c. Set bit at position (char >> 3) byte, (char & 7) bit using BTS instruction\n   d. Advance to next character\n3. Initialize counter to -1\n4. For each character in lpszString:\n   a. Increment counter\n   b. Read character byte value\n   c. If null terminator, return counter (entire string scanned)\n   d. Check if character's bit is set in bitmap using BT instruction\n   e. If bit set (character in charset), return counter\n   f. Advance to next character and continue loop\n\nParameters:\n  lpszString - Pointer to null-terminated string to scan\n  lpszCharSet - Pointer to null-terminated set of characters to search for\n\nReturns:\n  int - Index of first character in lpszString that matches any character in lpszCharSet,\n        or length of lpszString if no match found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty lpszCharSet returns length of lpszString (no bits set in bitmap)\n  - Empty lpszString returns 0\n  - Null terminator in lpszString never matches (loop exits before bitmap check)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 (32) - Size of bitmap in bytes (256 bits / 8 = 32 bytes)\n  >> 3 - Divides character value by 8 to get byte index in bitmap\n  & 7 - Masks to get bit position within byte (0-7)\n\nNote: This is a standard C library strcspn() implementation using a bitmap\nfor O(n+m) performance where n=len(lpszString), m=len(lpszCharSet).",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:30f0fd08cad97c1e8bd24ed371c4d8a2",
