      "name": "SyncStreamDescriptor",
      "signature": "int SyncStreamDescriptor(dword dwStreamId)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Synchronizes and closes a stream descriptor with thread-safe locking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate stream ID is within bounds (< g_nStreamCount)\n2. Calculate bucket index (dwStreamId >> 5) and slot index (dwStreamId & 0x1F)\n3. Check stream descriptor active flag (bit 0 at offset +0x04)\n4. If invalid stream ID or inactive, set errno=9 (EBADF), clear OS error, return -1\n5. Acquire stream critical section lock via AcquireStreamLock\n6. Call CloseStreamAndHandle to close file handle and free descriptor\n7. Release stream critical section lock via ReleaseStreamLock\n8. Return result from CloseStreamAndHandle (0 success, -1 error)\n\nParameters:\n- dwStreamId (dword): Stream index into descriptor table\n  - Bits 5+: Bucket index into g_apStreamDescriptors array\n  - Bits 0-4: Slot index within bucket (0-31)\n\nReturns:\n- int: 0 on success, -1 on error (errno set)\n\nError Values:\n- errno 9 (EBADF): Bad file descriptor - stream ID invalid or not active\n\nStream Descriptor Layout (0x24 = 36 bytes per entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  0x00    4     hFileHandle        OS file handle\n  0x04    4     dwFlags            Stream state flags (bit 0 = active)\n  0x08    4     nLockInitialized   Critical section init flag\n  0x0C    24    criticalSection    RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION structure\n\nIndex Calculation:\n  bucket = dwStreamId >> 5 (divide by 32)\n  slot = dwStreamId & 0x1F (mod 32)\n  descriptor = g_apStreamDescriptors[bucket] + slot * 0x24\n  flags = descriptor + 0x04\n\nThread Safety:\nStream lock acquired before close operation to prevent concurrent access during cleanup.\n\nCalled By:\n- FlushStreamInternal: After flushing buffer, syncs underlying descriptor",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f69087a4d0d613e8eb1a99e63a6b0789",
