      "name": "CloseStreamHandle",
      "signature": "int CloseStreamHandle(uint dwStreamId)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Closes a stream's OS file handle and invalidates its descriptor entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get the OS file handle for the stream via GetStreamFileHandle(dwStreamId)\n2. If handle is invalid (-1), skip to step 7 (already closed)\n3. If stream is stdout (1) or stderr (2), check if they share the same handle:\n   - Get handles for both stdout and stderr\n   - If handles are identical, skip CloseHandle to avoid double-close\n4. Call GetStreamFileHandle again to get the handle for CloseHandle\n5. Call CloseHandle(hObject) to close the OS handle\n6. If CloseHandle fails, capture error via GetLastError()\n7. Call CloseStreamDescriptor(dwStreamId) to invalidate descriptor's handle field\n8. Clear the stream descriptor's flags byte (offset +4) to mark as closed\n9. If no error occurred, return 0 (success)\n10. If error occurred, call MapOsErrorToErrno to set errno, return -1\n\nParameters:\n- dwStreamId (uint): Stream index (0=stdin, 1=stdout, 2=stderr, 3+ user streams)\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success - stream handle closed and descriptor invalidated\n- -1: Error - CloseHandle failed (errno set via MapOsErrorToErrno)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid handle (-1): Skips CloseHandle, still clears descriptor flags\n- Shared stdout/stderr handle: Skips CloseHandle to prevent double-close\n- Always clears descriptor flags regardless of CloseHandle result\n\nStream Descriptor Layout (0x24 bytes per entry):\nOffset  Size  Field    Type   Description\n0x00    4     hFile    int    OS file handle\n0x04    1     bFlags   byte   Stream flags (bit 0 = open)\n\nGlobal References:\n- g_apStreamDescriptors: Array of bucket pointers (32 entries per bucket)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1F: Mask for offset within 32-entry bucket\n- 5: Right shift for bucket index\n- 0x24: Stream descriptor stride (36 bytes)\n- 0xFFFFFFFF: Invalid handle sentinel",
