      "name": "FreeStreamBufferIfDynamic",
      "signature": "void FreeStreamBufferIfDynamic(int * pStreamState)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Frees dynamically allocated stream buffer and resets buffer state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if stream has active mode flags (0x83 mask: read/write/dirty)\n2. If active AND dynamically allocated (flag 0x08), then:\n   a. Free buffer at offset +0x08 via ProcessAllocatedMemory\n   b. Clear dynamic (0x08) and extended (0x400) flags via AND 0xFBF7\n   c. Reset buffer position (offset +0x00) to 0\n   d. Reset buffer pointer (offset +0x08) to 0\n   e. Reset buffer end (offset +0x04) to 0\n3. If not dynamically allocated, skip cleanup (static buffer)\n\nParameters:\n- pStreamState (int *): Pointer to stream state structure\n  - Offset +0x00 (dword): Buffer read/write position\n  - Offset +0x04 (dword): Buffer end position  \n  - Offset +0x08 (dword): Buffer pointer (freed if dynamic)\n  - Offset +0x0C (word): Stream flags\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nFlag Bits (offset +0x0C):\n- 0x01: Read mode active\n- 0x02: Write mode active\n- 0x08: Buffer dynamically allocated (cleared on free)\n- 0x80: Buffer dirty/modified\n- 0x400: Extended buffer mode (cleared on free)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If flags & 0x83 == 0 (no active mode), skips entirely\n- If flags & 0x08 == 0 (static buffer), skips free\n- Only frees when BOTH conditions are true (dynamic AND active)\n\nCalled by:\n- FlushStreamInternal: During stream flush/close operations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
