      "name": "__allmul",
      "signature": "longlong __allmul(uint dwMultiplierLow, int nMultiplierHigh, uint dwMultiplicandLow, int nMultiplicandHigh)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Performs signed 64-bit integer multiplication for 32-bit x86 code.\n\nStandard CRT helper function for 64-bit multiply when native IMUL is unavailable.\nTakes two 64-bit integers as pairs of 32-bit low:high words and returns 64-bit product.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if both high words (nMultiplierHigh, nMultiplicandHigh) are zero\n2. If both zero: simple 32x32 multiply (dwMultiplierLow * dwMultiplicandLow) returns in EDX:EAX\n3. If either non-zero: full 64-bit multiply using schoolbook method:\n   - Compute cross products: (high_A * low_B) + (low_A * high_B)\n   - Add to high word of (low_A * low_B)\n   - Result = low_A * low_B + ((high_A * low_B + low_A * high_B) << 32)\n\nParameters:\n  dwMultiplierLow   [ESP+0x04] - Low 32 bits of first 64-bit operand (A_low)\n  nMultiplierHigh   [ESP+0x08] - High 32 bits of first 64-bit operand (A_high)\n  dwMultiplicandLow [ESP+0x0C] - Low 32 bits of second 64-bit operand (B_low)\n  nMultiplicandHigh [ESP+0x10] - High 32 bits of second 64-bit operand (B_high)\n\nReturns:\n  EDX:EAX - 64-bit product (lower 64 bits of true 128-bit result)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fast path when both high words are zero avoids cross-product computation\n  - Overflow beyond 64 bits is silently truncated (standard behavior)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d54b31472f74b078be31f20f65c7b2d3",
