      "name": "UnlockFileHandleThunk",
      "signature": "void UnlockFileHandleThunk(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "C runtime file handle unlock thunk wrapper\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Push EBX to preserve file handle value on stack\\n2. Call __unlock_fhandle to release internal C runtime file handle mutex\\n3. Pop return address into ECX (discards it - unusual but valid for thunk functions)\\n4. Return to caller via RET instruction\\n\\nParameters:\\nnHandle (int): File handle value to unlock, passed implicitly in EBX register\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value. Function performs side effect of unlocking the file handle mutex.\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\nThis is a wrapper/thunk function used by the C runtime __write function to safely unlock a file\\nhandle after write operations complete. The POP ECX instruction pattern is unconventional - it\\ndiscards the return address rather than leaving it on the stack, but is valid for thunk functions\\nthat don't need to return to their immediate caller. The function's unusual control flow pattern\\nsuggests it may be used as part of an exception handling or cleanup mechanism.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d4c2d26a88b113bd75739659d4ef7dd5",
